2218	Planet Of The S	5203	Fruit Beer	4.8	\N	This is a new range of Special Edition beers we’re starting. Planet of the Ales will include our more experimental beers and as such we will have labels that depart from our norm to make them stand out. The first one out of the gates is a Pimm’s inspired fruit cup. It’s summer, Wimbledon will be upon us when this is released and what better way to celebrate than with a nice summer ale. What makes it a fruit cup pale, I hear you ask... Well to start with we boiled with orange and lime zest and fresh cut mint leaves. After primary fermentation we split the batch and added fresh strawberries to one third, a whole fresh cucumber to one third, and left the final third on it’s own. After another week like this we blended these together to get one hell of a fruity, cucumbery ale. I’m not expert on the taste of Pimm’s, but I’m told this comes very close, or at least as close as it can in a beer.[ NOTE: Please DO NOT remove the brewery name from the Twisted Barrel entries. ]	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:40.361767	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
