4621	Swing	258	Dortmunder	5.8	\N	It is called ‘swing’ because it has the instinct of this kind of music and its soft, sensual rocking motion. It has an independent character and motion with sudden notes of malt. It is the colour of ripe wheat in August. The fragrance notes are delicate but intense and lovable, with a touch of bitterness. This musical beer evokes an ever-present era with ancient traditions, reminding drinkers of guitars and clarinets. This very clear, golden, low-fermentation beer has a pleasantly bitter taste of hops and a yeast fragrance. It produces a good head of fairly resistant foam tasting slightly of hops. It is suitable at any time of the year and any time of the day.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
