4623	Blues	258	Dunkel	5.6	\N	It is a journey among the blue devils of music, vague memories, perhaps of something missing. There is more passion than melancholy in this round red beer that is part of our evening. The beer was born of emotions. It touches the soul and is difficult to forget. It is essential and caresses gently, a harmonious solo voice. Munich malt (which gives sweet notes of dry fruit, chocolate and caramel) is used to brew this low-fermentation dark beer, which is intensely reddish with a moderate hops note. It is pleasant to drink with other people or on your own.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
4624	Jazz	258	Dunkelweizen	5.5	\N	It is a winter beer that reminds drinkers of wheat, even after the harvest. Its amber colour that fades into autumn colours is mesmerising. A meditation drink, this beer should be drunk in company. Enjoy its unusual tones, like a soloist that rejoins the group after surprising you (saxophone, trumpet and clarinet). This soft, embracing, high-fermentation beer has a malted wheat base and is amber in colour. It combines the bitterness of a weizen with the roundness of a dunkel lager. The fragrance notes are banana, dried fruit and caramel. It should be drunk in the company of friends.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
4625	Country	258	Hefeweizen	4.8	\N	This soft turbidity contains the desire for coolness of hot sunny days, the welcoming heat of the foam that is great right into the autumn. This drink is for palates seeking an unexpected pleasure and includes the sensation of spinning dances, hands clapping in rhythm and laughter, with guitars and violins playing occasionally in the background. This high-fermentation beer with a malted wheat base is straw yellow in colour, very opalescent with a big head of foam. Its fragrance is intense. It is a bubbly, discreetly sour, fresh-tasting beer. The fragrance notes are typical of high-fermentation beers (banana, cloves and often bread crust and yeast notes as well). The easy-to-drink beer has a slightly citrus-like taste and barely perceptible bitterness. The wheat gives it a pleasant and refreshing sour taste with elegant fruit and spice fragrance notes. Drink this beer in cheerful company.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
4693	Ron Mexico (2015 National Homebrewers Conference Bottle)	259	American Pale Ale (APA)	4.5	\N	The Hop Breeding Co. (HBC) is releasing a new variety hop currently known as HBC-438. With a history that goes back to the late 1990s, HBC-438 is affectionately known as “Ron Mexico” after a pair of homebrewers were gifted some a decade ago. The name pays homage to the hop plant’s background, which is half neomexicanus. The hop has distinct notes of tropical and stone fruits, creating a delicious hop aroma in this session IPA brewed by Vinnie Cilurzo, owner and brewmaster at Russian River.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
