6144	- Alma Dannata	326	Tripel	8.0	\N	Birra ad alta fermentazione. Birra dannata è una zona affascinante e inaccessibile che ha segnato il birraio e la sua storia. Birra dall’aspetto gentile e cordiale, con tratti spigolosi e un’energia che viene dal lavoro in una terra estrema ma generosa. Una tripel luppolata, brassata con pazienza e amore. Servire a 8 - 10° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo, avena, zucchero candito, luppolo, lievito. 17,5° P. Tap Room Series.Top fermentation beer. Damned beer is a fascinating and inaccessible area that has marked the brewer and his story. Kind and friendly looking beer, with angular strokes and an energy that comes from work in an extreme but generous land. A hopped tripel, brewed with patience and love. Serve at 8 - 10° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, oats, sugar, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.839507	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6145	- Via Andante	326	Saison	5.5	\N	Birra ad alta fermentazione che ricalca le Saison classiche del Belgio. Lieve opalescenza con riflessi dorati sovrastati da una schiuma candida, densa ed abbondante di buona durata. All’olfatto un arsenale sensoriale ricco ed avvolgente, ben delineato, fresco e speziato con sensazioni pepate e tocchi di crosta di pane. Al palato un’immediata nota acidula, secca e speziata. La carbonazione è ben bilanciata da rendere la sorsata scorrevole, dal finale delicatamente fruttato (albicocca, canditi) e retrogusto persistente. Servire a 4 - 6° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo, malto di segale, zucchero, luppolo, lievito. 12° P. Tap Room Series. Top fermentation beer that traces the classic Saison of Belgium. Slight opalescence with golden reflections surmounted by a white, dense and abundant foam of good duration. On the nose a rich and enveloping sensory arsenal, well defined, fresh and spicy with peppery sensations and touches of bread crust. On the palate an immediate acidulous note, dry and spicy. The carbonation is well balanced to make the sliding sip, with a delicately fruity finish (apricot, candied fruit) and a lingering aftertaste. Serve at 4 - 6° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, rye malt, sugar, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.839507	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6968	10 Commandments	5246	Belgian Strong Ale	10.0	\N	Lost Abbey’s once a year Anniversary beer. A new generation of Dark Farmhouse Belgian-Style Beer that had Brettanomyces (a special Belgian brewer’s yeast) added at bottling. (from newsletter) (from bottle:  Ale Brewed with Raisins)  10 commandments:  1.  The most imaginative beers are our crusade.  2. We believe we are all in this together.  3. We strive for honesty and integrity in our lives like you.  4.  Fresh beer is great, aged beer is better.  5.Now that you have found us, help us spread the message.  6.  There is good and evil in the world, our beers are good.  7. Passion isn’t something you can buy at the corner store.  8. We believe an inspired life is worth living. 9. Life is about choices.  The Lost Abbey is a great choice.  10. We are not perfect but no one is.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6146	- E=Stiva	326	Specialty Grain	5.0	\N	Summer ale color oro. Birra dall’arsenale sensoriale ricco ed avvolgente, ben delineato, fresco, agrumato e speziato con sensazioni pepate e tocchi di crosta di pane. Al palato bilanciata tanto da rendere la sorsata scorrevole con un finale delicatamente rinfrescante. Freschezza e  secchezza da saison, piacevolezza da rye ipa, basso tenore alcolico e facilità di bevuta. Servire a 4 - 6° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo, malto di segale, avena, zucchero, luppolo, lievito. 11° P. Tap Room Series. Summer gold colored wings. Beer with a rich and enveloping sensory arsenal, well defined, fresh, citrus and spicy with peppery sensations and touches of bread crust. On the palate balanced enough to make the sliding sip with a delicately refreshing finish. Freshness and dryness from Saison, IPA rye pleasantness, low alcohol content and easy drinking. Serve at 4 - 6° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, rye malt, oats, sugar, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.839507	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
