7596	Pecan Pie Porter - 2010-2011	5252	Porter	7.0	\N	Pecans suck. That’s what I thought as a kid. Now I love them.So much so that I decided to create a beer in homage to the pecan as it find the perfect home: pecan pie. Our Pecan Pie Porter balances sweet and nutty porter flavors with the subtle addition of all natural and organic pecan concentrate and butter pecan extract. The result is mouth watering goodness.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.430466	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
7598	Pecan Pie Porter - 2016	5252	Imperial Porter	8.5	\N	Genghis Pecan begrudgingly entered a pie eating contest at our request and ended up truly enjoying himself, but he no longer fits into his armor.  For this year’s version of our Pecan Pie Porter, we tweaked the base recipe and added some honey malt for some additional sweetness along with the toasted pecans.  We raise a toast to Genghis Pecan, whose memory will live on as long as you are drinking this beer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.430466	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
