7256	Bygone	5250	Saison	6.6	\N	Belonging to an earlier time, Bygone is our journey back of an old world tradition. This tart saison blend is composed of 3 different oak barrels. Two barrels were solely fermented with DuPont saison yeast in primary and then underwent a secondary fermentation with Brettanomyces inoculations. One barrel was inoculated with Amalgamation, a Brett super blend, and the other with Brettanomyces bruxellensis. These two barrels were then blended with 1 oak barrel that was fermented with DuPont saison yeast, Brettanomyces anomala, and a belgian mixed culture. The result is a tart saison with a low acidity, with notes of pear, orange peel, pink peppercorn, and hay.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.22296	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
