9375	Boerinneken	443	Tripel	9.5	\N	A blonde, strong beer with a hoppy taste.Ingredients: Water, Malt, Hops, Yeast. Boerinneken 0.33 l. is a blonde type of abbey beer of double fermentation inside the bottle. Its taste is of somewhat sweet hops, with a volume percentage of 9.5%. The bottle is closed with a snap wing stopper. Brewed for ’Den Ouden Advocaat’, an artisanal producer of, primarily, home-made eggnog liqueur (advokaat) in Sint-Niklaas.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.005964	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11154	Patrons Projects 8.01 Ddh Lager Ekuanot	5288	India Pale Lager	6.0	\N	With the increased capacity of our new production facility freeing up a few vessels at our Old Flax Store site, brewing our first Lager style beers was always high on our list of ways to fill them up. Lager fermentations are a slower, more delicate process to which we previously could not commit tank time to, but which are a technical challenge we'd been itching to tackle. We're all still hopheads at heart as well though so we have attempted to find the perfect hybrid between IPA and Lager, putting together a series of single variety, dry hopped lagers showcasing hops we felt equally straddle the line between US citrus fruit and classic German noble character.First up is Ekuanot, a US hop which already is a firm favourite at NMBCo HQ making up a 1/3 of the dry hop of our flagship New World IPA. Once fondly known as 'Citra Plus' in brewing circles, Ekuanot packs a big tropical aroma of Papaya and Mango plus softer hints of Melon and Lime. It also has a noble-like delicacy and floralness which put it to the forefront of our mind for the series. The base beer is a classic German Lager in the main, utilising the softest brewing water with Pils malt backed up by aa touch of Munich for depth and Wheat for mouthfeel and head retention. Soft but prominent bitterness leading to a crisp, clean profile on which to layer the different flavours of our chosen hop.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11146	Dark City	5288	Milk/Sweet Stout	7.4	\N	There a few greater brewers of stouts and porters in Europe tan De Molen so we were delighted to welcome them back to Leeds for a second time to put together something suitably rich for the occasion. As you'd expect, this brew is all about the malt. Classic English Maris Otter malt acts as a base to many layers of complexity, starting with copious quantities of oats for mouthfeel. Three different crystal malts were also brought in to add notes of dark fruit, toffee and treacle to the flavour profile along with Munich malt for depth. Finally, Lactose to give the silkiest of drinking experiences, as expected of a milk stout.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11150	World Gone Sour	5288	Sour / Wild Ale	6.2	\N	For this Twist we brewed a soured version of our flagship New World IPA, introduced Citra to the existing hop bill of Simcoe, Chinook and Ekuanot and added Lemon juice for an extra level of zing.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11189	The Trilogy MMXVIII: Yeast	5288	Sour / Wild Ale	6.5	\N	The Trilogy MMXVIII - Yeast. Sour IPA collab with Verdant.Our Trilogy series is designed to showcase the three core elements that shape every beer you drink.From across the world, some of the true masters of these ingredients have come to join us at the Old Flax Store to pay homage to Hops, Yeast, and Malt.Each year we add a theme to the trilogy, whether it's geographical, the use of fruit or barrel aging, this family of beers will have common elements built into their DNA.In the third year of our trilogy series that DNA is IPA.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
