11164	Patrons Projects 8.02 Ddh Lager Citra	5288	India Pale Lager	5.7	\N	This Patrons Project beer is a collaboration with skateboard photographer Reece Leung, whose artwork is featured, and Vague, a magazine delivering skateboarding, art, beer and the rest.Second up in the series is a bit of a curveball - Citra. A regular in the NMBCo brew house (and many others) this hop lives up to its name. No hop delivers quite the tropical punch as consistently and overwhelmingly as Citra, making it a go to option for US-style IPA's. It's the softness of these flavours which brought it to the table for our DDH lager series. All of that tropical flavour can be delivered in the most super soft of packages. This means it actually partners well with the clean body of the beer and makes it perfect for Lager fans and hopheads alike!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11155	Rising - Raising The Faith	5288	American Pale Ale (APA)	5.5	\N	Triple Dry Hopped Pale Ale. http://www.northernrising.comWe’re giving you the opportunity to join us by owning a piece of our brewery. As many will now know, we have decided that this is the right time to raise money to accelerate our growth by letting you own a share of our business. Funds raised will triple capacity helping us meet demand. If we overfund we will fast track our plans to open tap rooms, with our sights set on London and Manchester. For us this is an opportunity to let likeminded people join us on our journey. We do not envisage doing it again.Read all about it on our blog: https://www.northernmonkbrewco.com/blog/2018/02/northern-rising-crowd-funding-our-approach	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11156	Patrons Project 6.05 Gluten Free Ddh Pale	5288	American Pale Ale (APA)	5.5	\N	6.05// GLUTEN FREE DDH PALE// CITRA, EKUANOT, AMARILLO, SIMCOE// JON SIMMONS// IT IS THE GREEN-EYED MONSTER WHICH DOTH MOCK THE MEET IT FEEDS ON// BURNT MILL// WHIPLASH. For this new series, it was great to be able to pull together two of the British Isle's up and coming breweries; Whiplash and Burnt Mill. The latter has brewed one of our favourite new beers of the past six months with their gluten free oat pale 'Steel Cut' and we were keen to see what we could do with the style once given the super-hopped approach of ourselves and Whiplash.1.5 ton of oat malt was hand-loaded into the mash tun to avoid the barley dust in the conveyer - good job there were six of us around to help! We added an extra dimension with flaked maize and sorghum, maltdrextrin for body and then went heavy in the whirlpool to try and layer in as much depth of flavour as possible. We dry hopped with all of the classic tropical fruit varieties too to make sure this brew really sings!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
