11858	The Beer Of Bengisu (By   )	508	Belgian Ale	6.0	\N	This is the second release by this small and dynamic micro-brewery operating on the shore of Lake Bosporus. What these two proud owners have achieved with limited tools and a lot of passion, is nothing short of exceptional. The Beer of Bengisu drinks like water in the Desert of Sinai and keeps you wanting for more. It is a Belgian Ale which surpasses its technical limits and its honey-taste (with a tinge of Bermudian rum) catapults it into a category of its own. It is ideally matched with white meats and fish but, truth being told, it is best alone, accompanied by a cold winter sun.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.944228	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
