11511	Orange Wheat	5291	Fruit Beer	4.6	\N	ORANGE WHEATCrisp, Tart, and Refreshing. Whole locally grown oranges added throughout the brewing process perfectly compliment this unfiltered wheat and barley based beer. Our oranges are purchased through the Old Grove Orange company (affiliate of the non-profit Inland Orange Conservancy) whose main objectives are to save the local orange trees from disappearing, spread the word about the local citrus growing heritage, and to feed the hungry with the unutilized oranges. Please visit them at www.inlandorange.org. All we need to do to save the orange trees is to eat locally grown oranges!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11513	Barrel Roll No. 04: Wing Over	5291	Barley Wine	11.2	\N	A well executed Wing Over is smooth and dramatic. This beer is no exception. Wing Over is a big, complex, American-style Barleywine featuring two English caramel malts and four American hops. Wing Over’s character is enhanced by dry hopping and then aging the deep amber liquid for six months in charred oak rye whiskey and bourbon barrels. Spicy aromas spill from the glass: rich caramel, citrusy hops, bourbon and oak. Layered flavors of toffee, vanilla, brown sugar, spice and rye whiskey lead to a warm and slightly bitter finish. This is a strong ale, meant to be sipped, savored and enjoyed.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11517	Alt-Bier Ale	5291	Altbier	6.0	\N	Caramel, Toasty, and Clean. This red ale is our unique version of anorthern German Alt-Bier. Enjoy silky caramel smoothness, followedby toasty, bready flavors and finished with a hint of chocolate roast.These flavors all come through in the aroma and combine in a trulyunique, very clean, complex, Alt-Bier.Additional Information:Our Alt-Bier is very traditional except for one twist, chocolateroasted malt. We decided to add the chocolate malt to add a littlemore complexity to the beer and for a perceived dryness that helpsto balance the caramel malty flavor.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11526	Local Fields: Warmer	5291	Spiced Beer	7.8	\N	This is a one-of-akind beer brewedfor the “cool”months of theSouthern Californiawinter. We blendtogether locallyharvested sprucetips from AngelusOaks, maple syrup from Wisconsin and cinnamon from Saigon injust the perfect amounts to complement each other. The base beerhas a nice rich flavor of malt and caramel which combines with thespices for a very well balanced and delicious beer.Additional Information:This beer was first produced in December of 2009 and the responsewas so good that we’ve decided to brew it each winter!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11521	Local Fields: Polycot	5291	Fruit Beer	7.2	\N	Polycot is a wheatbeer brewed withhundreds of poundsof organic apricotsgrown in SouthernCalifornia’s HighDesert. We brewthis beer during thevery small windowof time when the apricots are at their peak of freshness, usuallyearly July. The pureed apricots add a wonderful fruit flavor to thebeer and combine with the wheat for a refreshing tart finish. Thisbeer goes down smooth, but at over 1.5 times the alcohol of theOrange Wheat, it will sneak up on you.Additional Information:The name Polycot (Poly=Many cot=Apricot) is a modification of theoriginal name Paulycot. Paul-yicot was named for owner Ben Cook’sfriend Paul who provided the apricots for the initial batch. Hangar24 would also like to acknowledge and thank the many volunteerswho spend hours pitting (and de-stickering) thousands of apricots forthe brew. We couldn’t make this wonderful beer without you!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11522	Wheels Up Helles Lager	5291	Helles	4.3	\N	Traditional andSweet. This Munichstyle Helles bearsall its delicacies foryou to enjoy withnothing to hide.Sweet candy-likemalt sweetness anda hint of Germannoble hop flavor and aroma is what this craft lager is all about.Additional Information:When Ben (Hangar 24’s owner) and his wife Jessica were touringGermany on their Honeymoon they stopped at the Hoffbrau Housein Munich and were amazed when they tasted their Helles. Lighterbeers are normally boring, but well made Helles beer is definitely anexception and is now brewed for you in the only way Helles shouldbe enjoyed. fresh and local.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13482	Raspberry Leuven	5311	Fruit Beer	4.0	\N	We took our refreshingly tart Leuven and added a heavy dose of raspberries, about 16 pounds per barrel.  The result is a deliciously floral fruit beer that is dry and crisp.  Cheers to summer!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13443	Apricot Provincial	5311	Sour / Wild Ale	4.2	\N	Belgian-Style Sour Fruit Ale. We took a test batch of our sessionable sour summer ale, Provincial, and added a heavy dose of apricots. Notes of lemon zest and tart apricots.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11527	Seasonal: Oktoberfest	5291	Oktoberfest / Märzen	5.7	\N	Our fall seasonal isan ode to thebrewing traditionsof Germany. Thisamber lager isbrewed in trueReinheitsgebotfashion using thefinest imported German Malt, German Hops and German Yeast.Incredibly clean and balanced, this lager has a wonderful maltybackbone and a hint of earthy hops. Traditionally released in earlyfall, this beer will make you want to stand up and sing 'Ein Prosit!'Additional Information:The Oktoberfest in Munich started in 1810 as a celebration of thewedding of Crown Prince Ludwig and Princess Therese. The festivalwas such a hit that it turned into an annual event celebrated for 16days from late September to early October. Oktoberfest beer comesfrom the Marzen style. These beers were bigger, richer beersbrewed in March and stored in caves during the hot months ofsummer. In the fall, they were enjoyed at the Oktoberfestcelebration.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11528	Local Fields: Palmero	5291	Dubbel	7.0	\N	For our secondLocal Fields Seriesoffering we lookedto match a Belgianclassic with thesweetness ofSouthern CaliforniaDates. Palmero is atraditional AbbeyDubbel with a healthy addition of dates from the Coachella Valley.Fruity esters from the Belgian yeast strain combine with a delicatedate sweetness. This beer is full of flavors of caramel, raisin, rumand spice.Additional Information:“Palmero” refers to the title of a person that tends date palms. Wefelt this was a natural name for a beer brewed with Coachella Valleydates. The Coachella Valley is home to roughly 95% of all datesgrown in the US. Palmero (the beer) was designed to show off thewonderful complex flavor of Southern California Dates.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13430	Deceit	5311	Belgian Strong Ale	8.5	\N	This light-hued beer was inspired by Belgian Tripels and Golden Strong ales. A high percentage of Pilsner malt and a new yeast strain we used present a lemon character in the aroma. This citrus quality carries into the flavor and finishes with a slight tartness. This beer is well balanced and smooth, making it easy to drink and sightly deceptive because of its high ABV.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11574	Esb	5291	Extra Special Bitter	5.8	\N	An Extra Special Bitter made with Marris Otter and Golden Promise Malts, hopped with Fuggle and East Kent Goldings to provide the classic balance of the style. Moderately bitter, with earthy and floral hop aromatics. Finishes with lightly toasted malt flavors.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.944228	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
