12502	Brouwerij Okie	5301	Oud Bruin	7.0	\N	The first batch will be a 500 bottle release (750ml bottles) of a sour amber ale aged in red wine barrels. This beer was put in an open fermenter without pitching any yeast for 3 days. This allowed the beer to pick up wild yeasts that were in the air and ultimately they have contributed an amazing aroma to the beer. After the open fermenter, the beer was transferred to two oak wine barrels where a couple of strains of brettanomyces were introduced.The end result is a beautiful sour ale, with a wonderful, fruity, cherry aroma and a beautiful bottle that it has been packaged in. Letterpress of Tulsa used a print press to create every label. Since all of the labels are hand made, they vary from one to the other. Each label was then put on the bottles by hand, so everything about this beer is truly hand crafted.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.126897	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
12507	Oude Gueuze À L'Ancienne	5302	Gueuze	7.0	\N	Attention: from the brewer:The bottle version is called 'Oude Gueuze Tilquin à l’ancienne' and is 6.4% alc/vol (it is either in 375ml or 750ml), and the draught version is called 'Gueuze Tilquin on draft' and is 4.8% alc/vol.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.126897	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
12508	Oude Quetsche À L'Ancienne	5302	Lambic - Fruit	6.4	\N	The Quetsche Tilquin à l’ancienne (6.4% alc / vol) is a spontaneous fermentation beer obtained from the fermentation of destoned fresh purple plums (Quetsche véritable d’Alsace, close to the Damson) in a blend of 1 and 2 years old lambics for a period of 4 months. Unfiltered and unpasteurized, it is re-fermented in the bottle for a minimum period of 3 months. The lambics used were fermented and matured in our own oak barrels at the blendery. They are made from worts brewed by Boon, Lindemans, Girardin and Cantillon.The taste is slightly tart but also fruity and round which makes this Quetsche à l’ancienne may be more accessible for non-experts or less sophisticated palates. It also has a slight dryness from the skin of the plums. The nose perceives a plum brandy perfume.  First batch (2012) with a BB date of 23/02/2022 was made with ’Prune de Namur’ and limited to 500 bottles. Second batch (2013) limited to 5000 * 75cl and 10000 * 37,5cl was made with ’Quetsche véritable d’Alsace’.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.126897	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
