13054	Sã¸Le Kodama	5307	Schwarzbier	4.5	\N	A crisp German Schwarzbier, a dark and toasty style of lager, fermented and cold conditioned on French Oak for 6 weeks. Velvety, crisp, and complex. In the days of old, when lagers were cave aged and oak barrels were the de-facto vessel for holding most liquid, most lagers stored in this way would display the pointed tannic and vanillin qualities of their respective wooden barrels. Kodama is the first iteration of our exploration on the effect of wood aging in Lager production.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
