13438	Leuven	5311	Berliner Weisse	5.7	\N	Leuven was produced similar to a Berliner Weisse. After running the wort off into the kettle, we seeded with lactobacillus overnight. We then added Saison yeast and Brett C to the fermenter. The result is a refreshing tart saison with a massive citruy pineapple aroma with a hint of apple and clove. The flavor is noticeably tart without being overly sour. More pineapple and citrus flavors give way to a bit of earthy wet hay at the finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
16548	Jolly Rodger (2016 High West Barrel Aged)	640	Imperial Stout	10.2	\N	This limited edition beer started as last year's Jolly Rodger Imperial Coffee Porter that we aged in freshly empty High West Rye Whiskey barrels. After some exuberant sampling, we picked out our favorite barrels for tis final blend – and saved a few for later. We love the complex flavors of oak, rye spice, espresso, and chocolate dipped figs. Round, warming and comforting, it is meant to be enjoyed now or stored in your cellar for a few years.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.764883	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
