13519	Son Of Nothing	5311	Dubbel	8.0	\N	A delicious Belgian Dubbel born from the love between The Mayor of Old Town staff and Funkwerks.  Conceived while Brad was spooning Gordon (or Gordon was spooning Brad we try not get personal with those details)  after a night of too many Hofbraus at The Mayor.We flew to Belgium and snuck in late at night to scrape and cultivate yeast off the walls of the Rochefort brewery.  We were caught by the head brewer and had to kidnap him.  He is now dressed and posing as our bar manager.  Our former bar manager is somewhere now, we are not sure where.  If you see her let her know we wish her well.The Mayor and Funkwerks‘ collaboration beer ‘The Son of Nothing’, is now on tap at the Mayor. The Son of Nothing is an 8% ABV Belgian Dubbel. The name and logo are nods to the working title for Pink Floyd’s epic song Echoes which appeared on the album Meddle. Echoes was played during the tapping.The entire idea for the project originated while Kevin was spooning David Gilmour (or a poster of David, again…we do not get into the personal details)	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
