16914	Gravity Never Fails	5346	Porter	5.8	\N	Gravity Never Fails is a Porter fermented with a blend of two Belgian yeast strains. The beer will be dry with big chocolate flavors and a light roast character. We used an experimental hop called Warneton 7784. The hop was named after the Belgian town where the hop varietal was grown on a farm. The number, 7784, is the towns zip code. Nino really wanted to showcase this hop based on the malt profile he and Bob came up with. This lended to a much more hop assertive Porter.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.764883	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13575	Tap 5 Meine Hopfen-	5313	Bock - Weizenbock	8.2	\N	[Formerly Schneider-Brooklyner Hopfenweisse]TAP5 Meine Hopfenweisse shows how far wheat beer can go. This specialty was created by the crazy idea of a transatlantic brewing project between Garrett Oliver (brewmaster at Brooklyn Brewery, New York) and our brewmaster Hans-Peter Drexler. Tap 5 is a hoppy fireworks, a shiny golden, slightly reddish strong wheat doppelbock, with an intense floral aroma that reminds of tropical fruit and pineapple. An exotic fruity sweetness meets with fireworks of hops. This extreme wheat beer shows how far wheat beer taste can go and pairs very well with spicy food. Bottle conditioned.Ingredients: water, wheat malt (50%), barley malt (50%), hops (Hallertau Tradition, Saphir), yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.699996	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
