13670	Bourbon Berry Grove	5314	Barley Wine	11.5	\N	Bourbon Berry Grove is a burly wheat wine style ale. Brewed with copious amounts of local honey, carefully selected specialty malts, and pacific northwest hops. The aging of this brew in bourbon barrels with cherries and blueberries elevates the rich caramel/honey character to luscious heights. Pour into your favorite snifter, let warm, sip, and allow your belly to surrender in the comforting embrace of craft.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.699996	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13673	Baklava Braggot	5314	Mead	8.0	\N	This beer was not our idea, it was a suggestion from an imaginative customer who noticed that we brew a good amount of beers with honey and a few with walnuts. What a great idea for a playful beer inspired by a customer an an iconic dessert. 120 pounds of local honey, 15 pounds of local black walnuts, cinnamon, and the zest of 30 lemons make this beer truly unique. This beer is fermented with our house Belgian yeast strain to give it a touch of clove and some nice subtle fruity complexity. Beer should be enjoyed and remembered. This is why quality and character are at the heart of every beer we produce.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.699996	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13679	Hocking Tripel	5314	Tripel	8.0	\N	This 8% abc delight is crafted with Belgian Pilsen malt, white wheat, Crystal 10, and exclusively Saaz hops. The Cantrell Honey Farm in Athens, Ohio supplies gallons of locally harvested Golden Rod honey for this brew. The honey is added at the end of the boil to give this Belgian style triple an elevation in flavor and alcohol. The interplay of fruit/clove character from our Belgian yeast and the local honey is apparent but not aggressive. A shy departure from traditional tripels that is anything but timid.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.699996	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13687	Cabernet Barrel Aberrance	5314	Saison	8.0	\N	Aberrance is our black saison. We aged it in a Cabernet barrel for 6 months with a special blend of our house wild yeast/bacteria cultures and some critters from our good friend Chad at Crooked Stave. The Cabernet barrel added some great complexity and richness to the beer with some hints of funk, fruit, and a nice subtle tartness. At 8%, Aberrrance as a nice full and elegant character.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.699996	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
