14375	Cerveza De Mezquite	5320	Saison	5.3	\N	We’re pleased to introduce Cerveza de Mezquite — a farmhouse ale brewed with mesquite beans foraged from the Texas Hill Country!Mesquite beans have intrigued us for quite some time. We’ve long seen them growing on the mesquite trees all around us, but up until now, we’ve yet to make beer with them. Perhaps what intrigued us the most is their aroma, which we’d describe as having a brown sugar / molasses character. In this case, we took the beans (pictured below), hand-crushed them, and added them late in the boil.The base beer was quite simple, brewed on September 14, 2016 with malted barley from Blacklands Malt, malted wheat, rolled oats, and Goldings hops. Cerveza de Mezquite was fermented in stainless steel with our mixed culture of brewers yeast, native yeast, and native bacteria. It was packaged on October 19, 2016 and 100% naturally conditioned through refermentation in bottles and kegs. At the time of packaging, Cerveza de Mezquite was 5.6% alcohol by volume, 29 IBU, 4.4 pH, and 1.002 specific gravity (0.5 degrees Plato).Cerveza de Mezquite is dedicated to former Jester King brewer Ismael Salas.  Batch #2 -- January 2018 5.3% Mesquite beans from Sandeep Gyawali of Miche Bread in AustinPermíteme romper esta puerta matutina con valentíaY ser acariciado por su resplandor precozEncontraré mi Rocinante y heredaré el vientoSobre las espaldas de una cabra balandoDando saltos dulcemente más allá de las praderasAvanzando hacia un territorio más seco	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.888783	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
14376	Spon Albariño & Blanc Du Bois	5320	Lambic - Fruit	6.7	\N	SPON - Albariño & Blanc Du Bois is a blend of two year old 100% spontaneously fermented beer, refermented with Albariño & Blanc Du Bois grapes.Jester King SPON is inspired by the Belgian tradition of authentic Lambic and Gueuze. Wort from a turbid mash of well water, Texas malted barley, and Texas raw wheat was boiiled with aged hops from our barn, cooled overnight and innoculated with airborne yeast and bacteria in our coolship, spontaneously fermented in oak barrels for two years, and refermented for months in bottles resting on their side.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.888783	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
