19142	Scurry	5373	Traditional Ale	5.3	\N	Honey beer with molasses and oatsJust cause it’s dark and German doesn’t mean it’s an alt. Based on the obscure Kottbusser style of beer, this surprisingly dry beer retains all the aroma and nuance of honey (from bees) and molasses (not from bees) creating a perception of sweetness through cool, controlled fermentation. Because we’re sweet enough damn it. Grain Bill: Pils, Dark Munich, Chocolate Malt, Wheat Malt, Flaked OatsHops: Northern Brewer, Hallertau Hersbrucker, StrisselspaltAdjunct: Honey, Molasses13.5 Plato	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.608724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
