14481	Blue Quasar Amarillo Dry-Hopped	586	Lambic - Unblended	13.0	\N	The first Dry-hopped Ice Lambic Blend ever made.This is a blend of lambics, not a gueuze. 3Fonteinen from february 2008 and De Cam from 2005 make the base blend. A 15% of Mort Subite straight lambic from 2007 has been added to the base to obtain some extra sourness and to contrast the generous Amarillo dry-hopping, generating an extremely fruity blend. Then the blend has been freezed and the ice extracted.  The Amarillo was kindly brought by our friends at Pizza Port, in California. A special of the “Blackbird Series“, released only one time a year at the festival “Merla“ held outdoors in Montegioco, in the northern part of Italy on the coldest days of the year.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.888783	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
