15465	K-She-95 Kolsch	5329	Kölsch	5.0	\N	In honor of K-SHE’s 50th Anniversary we have created a smooth golden ale based on the classic Kolsch style. We use caramel malt and German noble hops to create a beer with a golden anniversary color and a smooth, balanced, flavor. You’ll enjoy this easy drinking everyday favorite that always pairs well with Real Rock Radio. Turn it up!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.252128	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
15467	Pineapple Wheach	5329	Fruit Beer	5.1	\N	We know you love your Wheach….we do too! The subtle peach flavor and aroma matches with the drinkability of an American wheat to make this beer perfect for many occasions…but there’s no reason to stop there. Just like our famous pumpkin recipe, we have decided to spice things up…pun intended. Pineapple Wheach is our latest spin on our famous Wheach beer. It’s the perfect blend of fruit flavors with a light yet crisp finish. Give Pineapple Wheach a try…you’ll be glad you did! Available on draught and exclusively in our Splash of Summer Variety Pack!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.252128	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
15468	Grape Escape	5329	Berliner Weisse	4.1	\N	Grape Escape Slightly Tart Beer is a wheat ale which is “kettle soured.” We add a blend of red wine grape juice to secondary fermentation to create a beautiful red grape hue along with a touch of flavor and tannin. You’ll find it light, refreshing and meant to quench the parched palate with a slight puckering finish...just tart enough!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.252128	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
15476	O’Fallon Dunkel Down	5329	Dunkel	5.1	\N	In the words of Ron Burgundy….. it smells of rich mahogany. This traditional German style, Dunkel is a malt-forward dark lager. Steeped in German history this beer was informally ordered as “Dunkel” referring to the darkest beer on tap. The Munich type malts used in Dunkel Down add the depth of rich toasted and nutty malt character with just a hint of sweetness. Traditional German Noble  hops add a hint of spicy bitterness and earthy character to the finish, while the lager yeast strain keeps this beer clean and crisp.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.252128	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
