15706	Birra Antoniana Con Grano Solina	615	Saison	4.5	\N	Birra dal profilo aromatico intenso, un corpo snello e un sapore fresco ed equilibrato. Con grano Solina dell’Appennino abruzzese, un’antica varietà di frumento tenero che cresce tra i 450 e i 1400 metri di altitudine, dove fin dal XVI secolo resiste al freddo intenso e alla neve su terreni poveri e ricchi di scheletro, e coltivato secondo i metodi previsti dall’agricoltura biologica. Servire a 6 - 8° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo, grano Solina (15%), fiocchi d’avena, spezie, luppolo, lievito.Beer with an intense aromatic profile, a lean body and a fresh and balanced flavor. With Solina wheat from the Abruzzo Apennines, an ancient variety of soft wheat that grows between 450 and 1400 meters above sea level, where since the 16th century it has resisted intense cold and snow on poor, skeleton-rich soils, and cultivated according to methods provided for by organic farming. Serve at 6 - 8° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, Solina grain (15%), oat flakes, spices, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.430276	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
