21679	Fear And Trembling	5413	Baltic Porter	9.0	\N	Fear and Trembling was Hill Farmstead’s first collaboration – a Baltic Porter brewed with malt that was hand smoked over maple wood by our Danish friend, and former colleague, Anders Kissmeyer. This version was a rebrew of Batch #4 in our brewery...and was aged for many weeks in stainless steel.  As a student of philosophy and former resident of Copenhagen, it is fitting that our brewer named our first collaboration after Denmark’s great thinker: Søren Kierkegaard. All three contemplated absurdity, faith, and salvation while wandering the shores of the Baltic Sea…“continue to work out your salvation with fear and trembling”Note: This is stainless steel fermentation, no barrel treatment (released 2013 and late 2015)	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.450619	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569529465841-dfecdab7503b?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
