24038	Half Tun Milk Stout Nitro	5441	Milk/Sweet Stout	6.0	\N	Our Two Tun Imperial Stout is a recipe that goes back to our Brewmaster’s days as a home brewer, and is brewed using just the thickest, sweetest part of 2 separate mashes (see what we did there?). To make the Half Tun, we collected the second runnings off a recent batch of Two Tun, a technique knows as “Parti Gyle” brewing. Then we lightened the hop rate and added some lactose. The result is smooth, sweet, and easy drinking, with notes of dark chocolate and a hint of coffee. Served on Nitro, its like chocolate milk for adults. Malts: 2 row, Bairds Carastan, Crystal, Roasted Barley, Black, ChocolateHops: EK Gold, Saaz, Cascade, Columbus	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.124448	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
