17679	Zwickel Bier (2016)	5356	Kellerbier	5.3	\N	You hold Brewmaster Dan Carey’s confident response to “What’s your favorite beer?” As a young Apprentice, this is the Reinheitsgebot Lager Dan brewed in Bavaria. Wisconsin glacial water softens a decoction mash of the finest Wisconsin, Czech and English malts. Dan personally selected the German, Czech and French hops for six separate hop additions. Finally, a long lager on his proprietary Munich yeast just as Brewers have done for 500 years. Straight from the tanks, unfiltered, this bier has undergone its third and final fermentation in the bottle in order to ensure you the freshest possible Lager bier. Expect this bier to be assertively hoppy, complex, and slightly cloudy. We revived the name but have brewed a new favorite that can only be found when you visit our little village Brewery here in New Glarus.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.105645	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
17685	Lucilla La Bianca	674	Blanche	4.7	\N	Birra Blanche non filtrata realizzata con malto d’orzo e di frumento, farro non maltato, scorza di arancia amara e coriandolo. Schiuma bianca, fine, compatta e persistente. Colore giallo paglierino velato. Al naso note tipiche dello stile: speziato del coriandolo si intrecciano con effluvi di lievito ed agrumi. Al palato: birra dal corpo leggero e piacevolmente acidulo e rinfrescante. Aromi di frutta e frumento. Abbinamenti gastronomici: pesce e carni bianche, insalate e verdure, formaggi a pasta filata e freschi. Birra dissetante e di facile beva, all’aperitivo con qualche crostino con ratatouille delicata di verdure o spiedini di pesce. Da provare anche a fine pasto con una spumosa crema al limone. Blanche unfiltered beer made from malted barley, malted wheat, unmalted Spelt, bitter orange peel and coriander. White, fine, compact and persistent foam. Veiled color straw yellow. The nose typical of the style notes: spicy coriander are intertwined with yeast and citrus scents. On the palate: beer from light-bodied and pleasantly sour and refreshing. aromas of fruit and wheat. Serving suggestions: fish and white meats, salads and vegetables, string cheese and fresh. Beer refreshing and easy to drink, aperitif with some toasted with delicate ratatouille of vegetables or fish kebabs. Also try to end your meal with a frothy lemon cream.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.105645	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
