17978	Costa Dei Villa	5359	Saison	4.6	\N	Costa dei Villa is a hoppy session saison that was brewed in collaboration with our friend Costa from La Sirène. These self-proclaimed ‘Farmhouse Free Stylers’ from the Land Down Under are creating amazing Farmhouse beers with finesse, texture, and above all crisp drinkability.This hoppy session saison was brewed with four different hop varieties giving aromas of citrus, kumquat, and soft wheat. Costa dei Villa is extremely quaffable, with a light tart body, and mild bitterness. Refreshing notes of grapefruit pith, a touch of Meyer lemon, and Jolly funk. The perfect beer for gathering the cobbers and sparking up the barbie!Come to my world mate!I’m going to finish my degree in marine biology and we’re moving to AustraliaI told my wife to beWell, that didn’t happen, I ended up a brewerBut not quite one of total ill repute.One Sunday in May Costa showed up at my breweryLater, we brewed a beer togetherCome to my world, mate, says heWe haven’t quite yetBut we will.Cheers & Mahalo plenty!Ron Jeffries, Founder and Chief Squeegee Operator	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.105645	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
