20492	Mi-Berry Vice	5394	Fruit Beer	5.6	\N	Mi-Berry-Vice is Pours a clear, raspberry red hue with a rose-colored head. Candy-like aromas of tart, red raspberry and snappy wheat malt. Fruit-forward flavors of blueberry, cherry, and red raspberry sit on top of a backbone of malted wheat. The beer is lighter-bodied than it looks and finishes clean and dry, which ought to make it appeal a little more to craft-beer drinkers, since it’s not quite as sweet as you’d think. Food Pairings: Berry pavlova, rustic fruit galette, tarts, other fruity desserts. Milky young chevre, sheep’s milk gouda, soft cheeses such as camembert. Salads, shellfish, poached salmon.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
