6616	Sand Creek	354	Double IPA	7.5	\N	Birra prodotta artigianalmente ad alta fermentazione, non filtrata e non pastorizzata. Dal colore ambrato e dalla schiuma morbida e compatta, la Sand Creek ha un aroma agrumato con note balsamiche e speziate che si ritrovano anche in bocca. Forti le sensazioni date dal malto con finale amaro, intenso e persistente con note di rabarbaro. In collaborazione con Fausto Marenco del Birrificio Maltus Faber, il nome della birra vuole essere sia un omaggio alla città di Genova e al suo massimo cantore Fabrizio de Andrè, sia allo stile americano dell birra ... in due parole: Sand Creek. Contiene glutine. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo (Pils, CaraVienna, CaraMonaco) luppoli (Columbus, Jarrillo, Centennial, Amarillo), lievito. Craft beer produced by high fermentation, unfiltered and unpasteurized. With its amber color and soft and compact foam, Sand Creek has a citrus aroma with balsamic and spicy notes that can also be found in the mouth. Strong sensations given by the malt with a bitter end, intense and persistent with rhubarb notes. In collaboration with Fausto Marenco of the Maltus Faber Brewery, the name of the beer wants to be both a tribute to the city of Genoa and its greatest singer Fabrizio de Andrè, both to the American style of beer ... in two words: Sand Creek. Contains gluten. Ingredients: water, barley malt (Pils, CaraVienna, CaraMonaco) hops (Columbus, Jarrillo, Centennial, Amarillo), yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6636	Peucet Levante	1397	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.7	\N	- Birra ad alta fermentazione– Stile: American IPA (America)- Denominazione e Grado alcolico: Birra doppio malto 6,7 % Alc. Vol.- Colore: ambrato- Abbinamenti: carni bianche e rosse anche alla brace, salumi, piatti piccanti e speziati, formaggi di medie e lunga stagionatura anche piccanti ed erborinati, pizze più elaborate– Contiene malto d’orzo Birra intrigante, dal colore ambrato con schiuma poco persistente. Accentuato aroma di luppolo con sentori floreali, fruttati e agrumati supportato delicatamente dal gusto del malto caramello. Corpo medio, moderata carbonatazione con un gradevole finale secco.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6638	Peucet Dark Sde	1397	Black IPA	6.4	\N	Nata da una collaborazione tra il Birrificio I Peuceti, il pub e beershop Birrarium di Acquaviva e il pub e beershop Corvo Torvo di Bitonto. Aroma – Prominente aroma di luppoli americani citrici, pinosi e agrumati, sentori di malto tostato, con lievi note di cioccolato e caffè.Aspetto – Marrone scuro con riflessi rubino e schiuma marrone chiaro.Sapore – un equilibrio tra agrumato, citrico, amaro, caramello, bassi sapori tostati, cioccolato e caffè. Bassa astringenza da malti tostati. Finale secco con caramello di sfondo. E’ accentuato il sapore di luppolo.Sensazione al palato – da leggero a medio, amaro da luppolo e leggero tannino da malti tostati si combinano per creare secchezza e pulizia.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6645	Idiot Ipa	5244	Double IPA	8.5	\N	It doesn’t take a genius to kno w quality West Coast IPAs require a stupid amount of hops. A generous blend of Nugget hops and the four Cs—Cascade, Centennial, Chinook and Columbus—brings forth a myriad of tropical fruit flavors and a brawny, persistent bitterness that makes for a highly intelligent brew.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6646	Islander Ipa	5244	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	Named after Coronado Island, our original India Pale Ale is a liquid expression of hometown pride. Centennial, Chinook and Columbus hops combine to provide an explosive burst of piney bitterness and luscious notes of apricot, grapefruit and mango that are sure to evoke imagery of swaying palms and sun-kissed shores.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6651	Sock Knocker Iipa	5244	Double IPA	8.5	\N	Amarillo, Centennial, Columbus and Simcoe hops unite to produce an immensely floral, botanical nose and a veritable explosion of citrus and pine on the palate. With an even more obscene hop overload than our infamous Idiot IPA, it’s an India Pale Ale truly deserving of its imperial crown.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6653	Hoppy Daze Ipa	5244	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.5	\N	CBC’s overriding mission is to brew beers that are 100% true to our San Diego roots. Our spring seasonal, an unfiltered Belgian-style IPA, does so in spades thanks to aggressive West Coast hopping, while paying tasteful homage to Old World flavors and brewing traditions.Previously listed at 9% abv	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6654	Stingray Imperial Ipa	5244	Double IPA	7.9	\N	Named after a serene Coronado shoreline where locals soak up sun and suds. This easy-drinking IPA will transport you to a tropical paradise the moment it hits your lips. Citra, Mosaic, Simcoe and Southern Cross hops provide flavors and aromas of tropical fruits and sun-kissed citrus with soft accents of nectarine and peach.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
6656	19Th Anniversary Imperial Ipa	5244	Double IPA	9.0	\N	What did we know when we set up a small brewpub on the island of Coronado 19 years ago? Not nearly as much as we know now!! Throughout CBC’s history, we’ve stayed thirsty for beer and knowledge, making each day into a learning experience. We’ve taken the time to hone our skills, maturing rather than aging. Our experience is evident in this double IPA. Hopped with Citra, Galaxy, Green Bullet, Mosaic, Nugget and Simcoe. Cheers to 19 years in the brewing business.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.026848	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
