8262	Ll Brew J	5257	Double IPA	8.8	\N	For our Natomas Head Brewer Jared Long, LL Brew J Double IPA is a West Coast homecoming. He grew up in Sacramento listening to 90s hip hop like Heavy D and you guessed it, LL Cool J, then later moved around the world before coming back to California. This West Coast-style DIPA is both a homage to California and a personal nickname he’s been wanting to see on a can for years (don’t get him started on Whitney Brewston). LL Brew J is dry and light in body, brewed with Simcoe, Mosaic, and Nelson Sauvin hops. For a Double IPA, it has a medium bitterness and light pineapple character. A hefty dry hopping gives it a deliciously dank aroma with a dab of white grape.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.622897	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
