9550	Fractal Motueka/Citra	5271	New England IPA	6.8	\N	This is the first time we ran a single IPA through our SOTL process and the result is a super-crushable single IPA that exhibits our signature EQ Juice.Fractal Motueka/Citra pours a resinous-hazy-yellow, releasing complex aromas of lemon-lime, pineapple, and tropical fruit. The taste is resinous dank sprite with EQ juice, keeping it refreshing all the way through to the finish. This one is a real crusher so please enjoy responsibly.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.195048	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
9551	Raining Belma From A Lactose Sky	5271	Double IPA	8.1	\N	Raining Belma From a Lactose Sky is a natural lyrical progression from Raining Belma, which starts with the same grain bill, supersizes the hop bill, and adds a touch of lactose. For this next tough-as-nails-beer in our heavy metal series we present you flavor and aroma: strawberries and cream over a citrus backdrop.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.195048	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
