11093	New World Ipa	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.2	\N	Cask, keg and bottle; Regular.Brewed at Hambleton until 7 August 2014, when Northern Monk’s own kit came into operation. A descendant of October beer, India Pale Ale is now one of the most popular styles in the world. Originally brewed in the 1700s by Hodgson’s Bow Brewery in London and exported to India by the East India Company. This beer has been through a 300 year evolution. Our New World IPA uses a combination of US, Australian and British hop varieties and is inspired by the hop ratios and techniques originally used.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11094	Eternal Session Ipa	5288	Session IPA	4.1	\N	Cask, keg & can; Regular.Our flagship beer is a World Beer Cup award-winning session IPA that’s low in ABV but high in hops. Appropriately named Eternal, this feather-bodied flavour bomb is fit to uplift your body and soul any time of day, any season of year.True to style, the recipe was envisioned to offer the hit of a generously hopped IPA, but with the sessionability of a classic English pale ale. Simcoe and Centennial hops dominate this light blonde beer with a swathe of tangerine aroma and a sublimely quenching citrus pith aftertaste that lingers on and on and on... eternally.Ingredients: water, malted barley, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11098	I Like To Moob It Moob It	5288	Double IPA	8.8	\N	A one-off, limited release beer. We joined forces with our Northern Brethren at Wylam Brewery to produce this moob-inducing answer to recent click bait articles about IPAs giving you man boobs. Now, we don't make science, we make beer. But here is what we know: there is no evidence that IPAs are giving you man boobs. Maybe it's true but maybe it's the end-of-the-night kebab, maybe we should go to the gym more often, maybe it's the peas, soya, dried fruit, chickpeas, beans (all of which have higher phytoestrogen levels than hops) maybe the whole thing was created by brewing behemoths making mass produced cheap beer with very few hops and losing share to craft brewers. One thing we do know, we like hops and we like to moob it.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11100	Mango Lassi Heathen	5288	New England IPA	7.2	\N	Inspired by the ﻿classic smoothie style Indian drink that refreshes and reinvigorates the senses, we elevated our flagship New England IPA with additions of mango and milk sugar for a delicious tropical treat.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11101	Patrons Project 6.03 Slamdank	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Our latest special release IPA harks back to IPA's gone by... Not English hopped but dank to the eyeballs like the classic West Coast IPA's that once dominated our drinking (many, many weeks ago....).We've aimed to take everything we've learnt and loved developing our NE-styles over the past year or so and bring the dankest hop varieties to the party. So the mouthfeel is still soft and silky smooth but this time with just a touch more intensity of malt flavour. A light bittering addition was backed up by heavy whirlpool hopping with Simcoe and Mosaic at reduced temperature for maximum flavour and minimal bitterness pick up.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11103	Hop City Ipa	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.2	\N	With Cloudwater.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11105	Patrons Project 13.01 Infinity Vortex	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Although we loved brewing 'Leeds Lurking', a Morello Cherry and Peruvian coffee imperial porter with the Other Half folks last year, this time around we just had to get hoppy!Not just that, but this year, we were delighted to invite Will & Ricardo from Equilibrium along as well. Fresh from pouring beer at Hop City, who, like Other Half, have been making huge waves in the New York brewing scene.This is the biggest IPA we've done to date with 30g/l of fresh Citra, El Dorado and Cashmere hops sacrificed in the name of maximum tropical juice and citrus zest!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11106	Double Heathen	5288	Double IPA	10.0	\N	Double Heathen, double the fun!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11107	Patrons Projects 5.01 Striding Edge Light Ipa	5288	Session IPA	3.0	\N	Our Patrons Projects to date have explored working outside of the classic four brewing ingredients, introducing different coffee, fruits and other additions more common to the culinary world, and all have also been very much towards the higher end of the ABV scale.All have tested the team as brewers in their own ways, but in 'Striding Edge' you could say we had our biggest challenge to date. With no fruit additions on the table and without the firm canvas that higher ABV gives, we set about creating a 3.0% ABV session beer with a flavour, intensity and mouthfeel of a drink of much higher strength. Starting with the base, we made sure our water was super soft and well balanced. Enough Sulphates to lift the hops, enough Chloride to smooth out the mouthfeel. For the malt we trialed a new Super Pale variety, making this by far the palest beer we have ever brewed, and made up 1/4 of the grist with Oats for the creamy mouthfeel they contribute. Ensuring the mash temperature was as high as we could go while ensuring some enzyme activity, we filled the wort with complex sugars to ensure a higher finishing gravity and consequently a chunkier body. We then layered in as much hop flavour across 3 dry-hop additions, going with west coast favourites Simcoe, Amarillo and Mosaic for an intense Pine, Grassy and Citrus character, backed up hints of Orange and Mango from a bonus Citra addition.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11108	Travel Notes	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	This floral, fruity IPA features five ingredients sourced from five continents, showcasing a world of extraordinary flavours explored in Lonely Planet’s Global Beer Tour. With Fieldwork.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11109	822 Double Ipa	5288	Double IPA	8.7	\N	Our beer draws inspiration from this very first reference of the importance of the collection of hops. The 822 IPA pays homage to the early days of brewing and showcases the best of today. Simcoe, Mosaic, Amarillo and Centennial hops all contribute to this resinous beer. Expect a fresh bouquet of hop aromas, with pithy citrus and pine notes on the palate, a rich, mouth-filling malt base and smooth bitterness.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11112	Patrons Project 2.03 City Of Industry	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.6	\N	For our latest limited release IPA we've continued to look at new ways to accentuate the soft fruit character of our favourite hop varieties.The grist includes flaked oats and wheat for mouthfeel and balance the water profile. We sought to reduce the bitterness pick up from out whirlpool hops by dropping the temperature at addition further which minimises isomerisation. We then selected our favourite headline US varieties Amarillo, Citra, Mosaic and Simcoe. Expect classic citrus fruit with underlying apricot, peach and subtle pine notes.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11115	Moobing On Up	5288	Double IPA	10.0	\N	MOOBING ON UP //TRIPPLE D HOPPED TIPA// CITRA, ELLA, VIC SECRET, ENIGMA, TOPAZ// BEN MATHER// WYLAMABV: 10%  10.00 EBC  IBU: 24  OG: 10.95. In 2017 we moobed it moobed it with our brethren at Wylam Brewery. The beer was celebration of hops and a middle finger salute to global brewing behemoths fuelling click bait articles about hops giving you moobs. It was a beer we enjoyed drinking. A lot. We’ve talked about bringing it back numerous times. In the year since we brewed I Like To Moob It Moob It we’ve both tweaked our approach to brewing IPA’s slightly and we felt like the time had come to brew the next generation. We’ve upped the ABV. We’ve upped the dry hop. We’re moobing on up.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11116	Glory	5288	Double IPA	10.5	\N	Now, what kind of a beer could stand shoulder to shoulder with an incredible Imperial Stout?A triple IPA called Glory, of course!Upon tasting it from tank, we were bowled over by the balance and how damn righteous this beer is. Bright, fresh citrus fruits absolutely shine in this brew.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11117	Patrons Project 3.05 Once, Twice, Three Times A Whale	5288	Double IPA	8.2	\N	We first brewed together at their home in NYC in June after attending Other Half’s Green City festival. The beer of choice was a double IPA utilising Citra hops in three forms; Leaf, T90 and Cryo Powder over a simple base of pilsner malt and flaked oats.Both parties were so delighted with the results when Kevin and Basil came over to the UK for London Craft Beer Festival, it only seemed right to continue the theme! This time we brewed the same beer but switched it up with Mosaic hops. Expect a silky combo of berry fruit notes, tropical mango and bubblegum flavour from this intense, multi-dimensional hop. Collab brew with Finback.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11118	Patrons Project 6.02 Knucklepuck Time	5288	Double IPA	8.5	\N	The 6.02 patrons release is a big hoppy double IPA brew in collaboration with American brewers Bissell Brothers and artist Jon Simmons. Packed full of Nelson Sauvin hops, backed up with Galaxy and Citra this hazy IPA punches big fruity flavours of gooseberry, passion fruit, peach and mango.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11119	Patrons Project 6.01 Hazemaker	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Amarillo Simcoe Columbus Exp035 with Deya and Verdant.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11120	Hop City Dipa	5288	Double IPA	8.4	\N	Northern Monk collaboration with Verdant, Deya and YCH Hops brewed for Hop City 2018.Double IPA brewed with Citra, Amarillo, Mosaic and HBC438 hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11121	Patrons Project 9.05 Eyeclops	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	One of the highlights of our first MBCC experience this year was meeting the great people behind some of the world’s best breweries (and cideries!) and sampling what they had to offer. A few people in particular that we got talking with inspired some new and exciting collaboration ideas, and this is one of them.On this occasion we have been lucky enough to welcome not just one, but two of these breweries to Leeds to brew with. First up we have Civil Society, a Florida based brewery who have perfected the art of bringing a little bit of Florida sunshine to all their beers! We have also managed to snag our second collaboration with Slim Pickens, the maker of cider and mead that tastes like the best juice you ever drank.We decided to brew a double dry hopped New England style IPA with them and we invited our guests to pick their favourite hops of the moment to headline the beer. Karl from Civil Society and Todd from Slim Pickens came up with the classy trio of Citra, Hallertau Blanc and Lemon Drop giving this IPA a sublime balance of citrus zest, grape juice and ripe tropical fruit over a super smooth oat-heavy base.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11134	The Trilogy MMXVII: Hops	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	A Rye IPA collaboration with DEYA Brewing Co.Our annual Trilogy Series is designed to showcase the three core elements that shape every beer. From across the world, some of the true masters of these ingredients have come to join us at the Old Flax Store and pay homage to hops, malt and yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11122	Patrons Project 3.02 Tropical Death Party	5288	Black IPA	10.0	\N	Pina Colada Black IPA We thoroughly enjoyed our first collaboration with Siren back in September, and once we came up with the Tropical Death Party idea (possibly the first time we've named a beer before deciding what it was even going to be) we instantly decided we should invite them back to help us step up the recipe. Wishing to push ourselves and our equipment to the maximum, we've turned the ABV up to 10, filling the mash tun twice to the brim to squeeze out every molecule of fermentable sugar we could. Then, as we both agree on one thing with the Black IPA style, we wanted all the colour with as little roast as possible. Cue a new technique for both of us, cold-steeping all the colour separately. Hops - lots of Sorachi Ace, famous for it's coconut notes, backed up with plenty tropical juice in the shape of Mosaic and Vic Secret. To seal the deal, double the Pineapple and Toasted Coconut to our previous work. Thick to the point of viscous in body, silky in the mouth with milk chocolate and coconut and finishing with a tropical punch.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11123	Patrons Projects 3.04 Attack On Blue Falcon	5288	Black IPA	7.0	\N	Blueberry & mosaic black IPA. This Black IPA has been in the back of our minds for close to a year now. We've always enjoyed how well Mosaic hops and Blueberry work together, really bringing out the deep, dark fruit character of the hops rarely appreciated in a lighter IPA.Blue Falcon showcases 20kg of the former and 30kg of the latter over a dark-as-night, round and silky malt base with copious oats and a sprinkling of Carafa in the mash and then darkened with the minimalist of addition of roast flavour.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11125	Eternal Darkness	5288	Black IPA	4.1	\N	Black session IPA. Limited release.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11128	Patrons Project 2.05 Lost Highway	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	2.05// PASSION FRUIT, MANGO, MILK SUGAR & VANILLA IPA// CITRA, MOSAIC, VIC SECRET, EL DORADO// NOMAD CLAN// LOST HIGHWAY// 7 ISLAND7 Island are one of the rising stars of European craft brewing who we were delighted to bring over from Greece to pour at their first international festival, Hop City, off the back of great results in the RateBeer awards. They were really keen to brew a fruited 'milkshake' IPA as laws back home prevent them from doing so themselves. This beer ticks all of those boxes, with both mango and passionfruit added to boost the tropical notes of Citra and Mosaic hops. We then added vanilla to compliment the smoothness brought to the style by lactose milk sugars.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11129	Patrons Project 3.01 Attack On The Bounty	5288	Black IPA	7.4	\N	A piña colada style Coconut Black IPA in collaboration with Patron tattooist/illustrator James Butler	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11130	Patrons Projects 4.03 Ddh Double Mango Lassi Ipa	5288	Double IPA	8.7	\N	It was always going to happen... Double Mango Lassi.More than double, in fact, as we upped the mango dosage by 120%.A super pale grist, heavy with oats and enhanced with slightly ludicrous amounts of lactose. We dropped the whirlpool to 80c before loading in the first addition of Citra and Mosaic. 18g/l of the same with added Amarillo following in dry hop before conditioning the brew with even more mango for a further week; letting the fruit settle in to complete the perfect alcoholic fruit smoothie in a beer can.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11132	Patrons Project 6.06 What Fools These Mortals Be	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	Edge Brewing based in Barcelona we believe were the first international brewery we visited for a collaborative brew and it’s taken this long to finally get them over to the UK for a return! We decided to try out a new IPA style that we’d been hearing about – Brut IPA. Enzymes break down all of the complex wort sugars into easily fermentable glucose, resulting in a bone-dry IPA backed up by high, sparkling carbonation.Another avenue we’d been keen to go down for a while was brewing with grapes alongside one of our favourite but hard to source hops, Nelson Sauvin. This felt like the perfect opportunity. We fermented this IPA with a Kolsch yeast strain – super clean and highly attenuative; then added 20L of white grape juice per barrel and double dry-hopped with Nelson Sauvin. The hop line up was then backed up with Halllertau Blanc, Citra BBC and Ekuanot Cryo pellets for a soft but crisp, resinous IPA full of juicy grape, elderflower, apricot and lime zest flavours.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11133	Dark Arches Black Ipa	5288	Black IPA	6.7	\N	An Oxymoron? Counterintuitive? Controversial? Black IPA marries the toasty dark malts of a stout with the hop punch of our New World IPA. Seen as an invention of the US craft movement, others believe the beer has its roots in centuries of British brewing tradition. Too dark to be an IPA, too hoppy to be a Porter, this beer is heavily dry-hopped with US and New Zealand varieties for a scintillating aroma of pine and tropical fruit Hints of toasted malt mix with big layers of US hop character from the addition of Simcoe and Mosaic Varieties.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11137	Patrons Project 5.05 Watching Crag Ddh Black Ipa	5288	Black IPA	6.6	\N	Moor Beer, led by Justin, have been great inspirations to us over the years with their progressive approaches to canning, their unfined and super flavoursome brews and creative styles. Above all, they’re great advocates for the black IPA style!When we finally got together to brew something it was inevitable that this would be our style of choice. We chose to follow a method neither of us had in our black IPA endeavors to date, with no dark malts going into the mash tun whatsoever. We added a portion of sinimar to the whirlpool and then topped up further in the fermenter. The result is a black IPA as we believe they should be – brimming with hops! We used a blend of our favourite, classic varieties of Centennial, Citra, Mosaic, Simcoe, Vic Secret for a balance of soft tropical fruit, resinous pine, and zingy citrus!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11138	Patrons Project 9.02 West Yorkshire Dipa	5288	Double IPA	8.2	\N	A continuation of our Northern Comic Book Heroes collaborations with illustrator Ben Mather. This time our buddies at Siren came down to give us a helping hand. This Double IPA is a hark back to old school West Coast brewing. Expect citrus and tropical notes, with a lasting bitter finish (I know right?!).	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11141	Patrons Projects 4.02 Pineapple And Grapefruit Juice Ipa	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.2	\N	For the second in our tropics-inspired series with Drew, we took inspiration from a popular soft drink (sounds like tilt...) to create an IPA packed with zesty refreshment. We've dropped the lactose right down from part one of the series aiming for a slightly crisper but still soft and round mouthfeel. Our chosen hops were Comet and Chinook for classic west coast grapefruit zest hop flavour, and a new variety - Denali. Developed by Hopsteiner, it's aroma notes included stone fruit, lemon and primarily, for the purpose of this beer, pineapple, so we were excited to give it a go. Grapefruit juice was added to the boil before we loaded the FV with pureed fruit mid-fermentation. Two dry-hop additions followed and a lengthy conditioning period at 10 Celcius to let the hops do their thing and to allow the fruit flavours to round out through the beer. Hopefully this beer delivers exactly as promised on the tin. Big aromas of grapefruit and prominent up front zest, the juicyness of the pineapple rides underneath with the classic long hop bitterness cutting through at the end. We'd like to think this is the perfect beer for the beginning of a long tropical British summer!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11142	Patrons Project 9.01 Captain North	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	We took advantage of our Cornish friends Verdant being in town to commence a new series of IPAs celebrating 'Northern Heroes'. We shot for good drinkability but all of the mouthfeel you'd expect, utilising an English yeast strain full of soft Apricot esters to support a hop bill designed for stone fruit flavours. Add in the unique gooseberry, white grape character of Nelson Sauvin and you have an elegant balance of soft fruit but hop punch, with peach, passionfruit and pineapple notes all shining through.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11148	Patrons Projects 5.02 Helvellin Ipa	5288	Session IPA	5.0	\N	As the altitude grows, so does the beer. We've stepped up from the success of Striding Edge to a 5.0% IPA for the second of our Ricky Lightfoot collaborations. The aim was the same though, just how much body and flavour could we build in to defy the ABV? Once again Oats make a large portion of the grist to boost that silky mouthfeel and we've also gone heavy on the Vienna, a base malt treated at slightly higher temperatures than normal to give a more prominent biscuit flavour profile and good body contribution. We've mixed up the hops as well and taken the opportunity to try out some new combination. There's some classic US citrus contribution in the shape of Amarillo and Ekuanot to back up a relatively new variety out of Germany - Huell Melon. You can probably guess it's primary flavour profile, which we expect to shine through after a couple of lengthy dry-hop additions.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11149	Patrons Project 3.03 Black Hole Sun	5288	Black IPA	6.8	\N	DDH Clementine Black IPA. James Kemp has lead the way with developing the Black IPA style ever since his days at Thornbridge and needs to take a lot of responsibility for my own love for the style as a result! We've worked together a number of times over the last few years but a Black IPA is one style we'd never actually got round to brewing, until the opportunity to collaborate with JK and his current brewery, Marble, for Manchester Beer Week came around.We decided to go 'juicy' and soft, giving our dark take on the NE IPA style. Copious oats in the grist alongside super soft water to give us the mouthfeel, some Simcoe hops at flameout for a depth of classic dankness then a double dry hop of Amarillo and Mosaic for all the soft orange, mango and dark berry. As a final squeeze of juice, a load of pureed Mandarin went in at the end of fermentation, perfectly complementing the hops and the soft fruit and sherbet tones of our house yeast. For the colour, a small amount of Carafa Spezial III in the mash tun and then a first experiment with Weyermann's Sinimar to darken the beer with minimal dark malt flavour contribution.This beer had been christened 'Black Hole Sun' weeks before brew day and before we even had a recipe. Come the day and our sparge is interrupted by the news of Chris Cornell, of Soundgarden, sadly passing away.We hope our creation is a suitable tribute. With Marble.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11158	Patrons Projects 4.01 Passion Fruit Lassi Ipa	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Canned & Keg;	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11159	Patrons Project 6.04 Hit & Roll Peach Lactose Ipa	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	This beer is the result of a long-overdue team up with our Danish brother, Soren of Dry & Bitter, Copenhagen. It has all of the peaches (peaches for me). For our first IPA together, we decided to accentuate the natural esters of our house yeast with 150kg of pureed peach and back it up with a subtle amount of lactose for a hint of classic 'Peaches & Cream'. For hopping, we combined the tropical notes of Citra and Denali with Simcoe and Wai-iti, both of which we have picked up stone-fruit notes from in the past.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11160	Patrons Project 13.02 Celestial Motion	5288	New England IPA	7.4	\N	For this series, we’re continuing the theme exploring the world of DDH IPAs and after the incredible feedback, we received from Infinity Vortex (the previous release in this series) we knew we had big boots to fill!This is another big double dry hopped IPA, just how Tank likes them! We have used a classic wheat and oat-loaded, soft New England style base to ensure a rounded mouthfeel which we then whirlpool hopped with Mosaic and Simcoe for a piney, resinous backbone.We fermented this beer with WLP008 East Coast yeast which is actually a new experiment for us! We selected this yeast due to its ability to emit loads of juicy citrus esters whilst leaving a nice residual sweetness. The 24 g/l dry hop featured yet more Mosaic and Simcoe, backed by the orange citrus, floral notes of US classics Amarillo and Cascade.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11163	Eternal Infinity	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Keg & Can;	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11166	Patrons Project 3.06 A Whale Of Two Cities	5288	Double IPA	8.9	\N	Meeting the Equilibrium guys at Hop City, our hop forward festival back in March, was one of the highlights of our year (their dancing at the after party will live long in our memory), as was the beer we made together - Infinity Vortex! It was great to welcome Will and Pete back to Leeds in October to get our brew on once again, and if it ain’t broke...We decided straight away to brew another big double IPA; this time showcasing the brewhouse’s favourite hops in the form of Mosaic and Citra. We then paired that time-honoured duo with the underrated El Dorado variety and the classic citrus and pine notes from Simcoe lurking underneath. Expect a riot of tropical fruit flavours over a classic, smooth New England base packed with wheat and oats.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11169	Magic Rock Patrons Project 4.04  Tropics	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	VICTORIAN LEMONADE IPAThe guys who started Magic Rock have been friends with some of the brew team here since before either brewery existed, but somehow, we had never made a beer together!Well, watch out world, because it's finally happened!On a base of extra pale, 25% wheat and a touch of acidulated malt to accentuate the acidity of the lemon, we went hard with 'all the good hops' to bring out a heavy citrus character; hitting the whirlpool with Citra and the dry hop with Citra, HBC438 and Lemondrop (see what we did there?!) We topped this up with lashings and lashings of lemon comminute to give us a delicious and refreshing drink to bring you back to your youth.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11172	Patrons Project 9.03 Don'T Look Baterang In Anger	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.3	\N	9.03 // IPA // VIC SECRET, CITRA, ENIGMA, DENALI // BEN MATHER // NORTHERN HEROES // DON'T LOOK BATERANG IN ANGER //Our good friends Track Brewing from Manchester came over to Leeds to play and continue our series of IPA's celebrating 'Northern Heroes'.Also the description is missing a paragraph, add this to the end:Our aim was a massively drinkable beer with huge body, utilising malted rye flakes and an American yeast strain full of peach and stone fruit esters to support a hop bill designed to elicit tropical fruit flavours. The international super star array of hops bring a palate of pineapple, peach and citrus designed to give you a beer that's the hero you deserve, even if it's not the one you always need, our kid.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11173	Patrons Projects 10.02 Raspberry Ripple Donut Ipa	5288	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.3	\N	10.02// DDH RASPBERRY RIPPLE DONUT IPA// RASPBERRY, VANILLA, MILK SUGAR, HUELL MELON, MOSAIC, BELMA, CITRA// TEMPLE COFFEE & DONUTS// CULINARY CONCEPTSFor this culinary concept we looked to take inspiration from Temple Coffee & Donuts with their creatively flavoured donuts that have truly captured the people of Leeds' imagination! With their creations in mind, we decided to combine one of our favourite flavours of our youth and inject a playful sense of fun into the beer whilst also looking at how to deconstruct those raspberry ripple dessert flavours into beer form.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
