15994	Black Fuel	629	Black IPA	10.5	\N	With a mighty roar, shiftless train engines make weak legs tremble and the black smoke billowing from their pipes dwarfs the sky. Prepare for a new, bitter race all the way up to the degree where blood boils – Black Fuel!In the grand line of fiercely hopped and vigourous IPAs, we turned to the rigid aesthetics of the tracks for inspiration, churning our new variety in a deep black with a dense bitterness. Despite a thick colour, notes of burnt malts are nowhere to be found, giving way to a coniferous and citrus of aromas and a quenching, dry taste.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.430276	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
16001	Rokot	629	Double IPA	8.4	\N	Cryo DDH Imperial IPA / ABV 8.4% / IBU 50 / OG 20.0 °PCryogenic temperatures were on track to reach maximum levels but then, Houston, we found ourselves a Rokot: our new Imperial IPA dry hopped exclusively with loads of lupulin pollen!For this one we used lupulin from Simcoe, Mosaic and Citra hops, which gives off a powerful citrus-tropical aroma that doesn’t taste too bitter. We threw in oat flakes for balance and fermented the batch with the Coastal Haze Ale Yeast liquid yeast strain, brought in from the American outfit at Copenhagen’s White Labs.A rumbly aroma with a pleasant balance of hoppy bitterness and a light sweetness.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:45.430276	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
