19733	Two Captains Double Ipa	5378	Double IPA	8.5	\N	English: Jan Halvor Fjeld, winner of the Norwegian home brewing championships 2010 brewed his champion Imperial IPA at Nøgne Ø. We at Nøgne Ø are of course proud to be with him in making this happen.Ingredients: Grimstad water, malted barley, hops and English ale yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19734	# 500 Imperial India Pale Ale (Batch 500)	5378	Double IPA	10.0	\N	Nothing is like celebrating your own milestones. This is a celebration of our 500th batch of ale. It was brewed with joy and splendor; the brewer wore a suit, and a TV station filmed the event. As a base for this ale, we have elected to play with numbers: 5 hops, 100 IBUs, 10% alcohol by volume. Indeed it is an Imperial India Pale Ale. Big and bold. Great for a celebration!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19753	Dobbel Ipa	5378	Double IPA	8.5	\N	Norge og Sørlandet har siden 1864 hatt innflytelse på brygging i Japan. http://www.kirin.co.jp/daigaku/o japan/william copland/index.html. Vi på Nøgne Ø ønsket å markere dette ved å invitere bryggermester Toshi Ishii fra Karuizawa, Nagano til å brygge sammen med oss. Resultatet ser du her: en Dobbel IPA.A guest brew by Toshi Ishii from Yo-Ho Brewing, 100 IBU.[Editor’s note: Released at EBF, september 12. 2008]	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19756	Vic Secret Ipa	5378	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.5	\N	Vi har klart det igjen! Å få tak i en ny spennende og denne gangen virkelig sjelden humletype. Vic Secret er bare helt nyyydelig med enblanding av frukt og furunål, som verden hittil ikke har sett maken til. Denne gangen har vi latt amerikansk vestkyst bestemme maltkomposisjonen i denne IPA’en. Det er gøy å komme litt ut av komfortsonen sin!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19762	Single Hop Citra Ipa	5378	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	According to the brewer, a British style IPA (90% Maris Otter, 10% Crystal malt) with American Citra hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19763	Citrus Hystrix Ipa	5378	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.5	\N	Citrus Hystrix er en India Pale Ale med rug, havre, bergamotblader, mandarinsaft og masse humle. Vi har rett og slett prøvde å finne noen gode smaker! Smaksprofilen på denne IPA’an er utviklet i samarbeid med Trond Moi.English: Citrus Hystrix is an attempt to put new and wonderful flavors in an IPA. To do this we added, rye, oats, kaffir lime and some tangerine juice! Taste profile of this IPA is developed in cooperation with chef Trond Moi.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19770	Mandarina Ipa	5378	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.5	\N	Imagine that the German have come up with a high alpha fruity hop! 'Could that be right?' we asked ourselves. We were in luck to get 100 kgs. The new wonder hop bears the name Mandarina, and it’s presently not commercially available. And how could we present this hop with all it’s glory? By brewing an IPA of course. Please welcome Mandarina IPA.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19782	Rd Jul	5378	Double IPA	8.0	\N	A well crafted holiday ale is to be savoured with all the senses. Listen to this ale come alive as you pour it into your glass. Feel the aromas of apricots and figs fill the room with holiday spirit. Let the flavors of tropical fruits seduce you. This is what the holidays are all about; pausing to take in the full ambience and impressions of the season.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19817	/ Alebrowar Chmiel Iunga Ipa	5378	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	Vi har mange venner i mange deler av verden. Så også i Polen. Her ble vi oppmerksom på en gammel humletype, nesten glemt, med masse herlig aroma. Iunga heter den. Vi traff til og med bonden som dyrker den. En hyggelig kar.'Men vi kan da ikke brygge et polsk øl alene' argumenterte vi. Michal Saks fra AleBrowar i Gdansk stilte opp, og i fellesskap har vi laget denne flotte IPA’en. We have many friends all over the world. Poland is no exception. Here we became aware of an almost forgotten traditional aromatic hop called Iunga. We even met the hop farmer - nice guy! But surely we shouldn’t brew the beer on our own. Michal Saks from AleBrowara in Gdansk volunteered to come to Norway and together we brewed this fantastic IPA.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.77706	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
