20770	The Black Pale	5399	Black IPA	4.5	\N	Traditionally dark beer flavours come from a high content of roasted malts and a low hop content. However, The Black Pale turns this on its head and goes for the best of both worlds, bringing together punchy hops and roasted malts.The hops give The Black Pale dark fruit aromas and flavours like blackcurrant and blackberry, plus a hint of pepper. The roasted malts add liquorice, raisin, caramel and coffee notes. The flavours are strong; they clash and combine to create a beer of real complexity but one that at 4.5% alcohol is also easy to drink.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.120099	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
