22786	Rollover	823	Session IPA	3.8	\N	Same hop rate of the DIPA, less than half the alcohol. A very heavily hopped Session IPA: this comes at you with buckets of Simcoe, Equinox, Citra and Mosaic with a light touch of malts and an easy crushable body. Previously brewed at Rye River.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22787	Bone Machine	823	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.2	\N	Bone Machine is our straight-up modern American IPA. Beginning with super soft water its grist is over 60% Oat and Wheat Malt layered onto biscuity and complex British Floor Malted Pale. 100% Whirlpool hopped with Oregon Cascades, fermented on English ale yeast and finally double dry hopped- with Ekuanot and brand spanking new BRU-1 hops.Candied Lemon. Resin. Papaya. Pineapples. Silk	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22789	Let It Happen	823	Double IPA	8.0	\N	Citra DIPA. Contains : Maris Otter Barley, Wheat Malt, Oat Malt, Citra.CITRA. CITRA. CITRA.Let It Happen takes our Saturate treatment and applies it to fresh bright Citra. 50% Oat and Wheat Malt, Floor Malted Maris Otter, super soft water, juicy English Ale Yeast and 100% Whirlpool hopped with Citra before undergoing 4 stages of heavy dry hopping riding up to 25g/L or tropical juicy madness.Unfiltered and unpasteurised as usual.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22790	Northern Lights	823	Session IPA	2.8	\N	Northern Lights – a 2.8% ABV 'Micro IPA' or Table Beer in a very very modern interpretation of the style. An an ode to the Seshlords of Yorkshire and the North of England beyond. Northern Lights builds on a base of German Vienna malt with heavy doses of Flaked Oats and Wheat along with a touch of Caramalt. Mashed super-hot with a particular process in our mash mixer we’ve done a decent job of retaining a huge amount of body and drinkability for such a low ABV beer. Hopped heavily in the whirlpool with Mosaic, it’s then fermented on London Ale III yeast before being dry hopped in two stages with Mosaic and Vic Secret respectively at a total of 16g/L.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22791	Do You Wanna Touch Me	823	Double IPA	8.3	\N	Wylam came round a few weeks back and they’d hear nothing of brewing anything other than an absolute monster of a Double IPA, which is pretty cool with us.This one uses Maris Otter, Oats, Carapils and some Belgian candi sugar to spring an absolute assault of Vic Secret and Citra in the whirlpool. She’s then double dry hopped with Citra, BRU-1, Vic Secret and Galaxy respectively. Fermented on London Ale III for a very foggy affair indeed.What you get is buckets and buckets of pineapples, mangoes, passionfruit and a touch of dank. All of which is complimented by a silky and creamy body with a light sweetness to finish. This one's a belter, and frankly we're just delighted we survived a weekend with Wylam.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22793	Swoon	823	Double IPA	8.0	\N	A big, dirty, jammy banger rocking at you with our usual lineup of Floor Malted Maris Otter, Wheat, Oats and then hit with Vic Secret and Chinook in the Whirlpool.This one’s been fermented on London Ale III – a bigger bodied, silkier affair altogether than our usual mix mash of DIPA yeasts. Then dry hopped with Vic and Chinook again, and again, and again until we crashed her then banged it into kegs and cans.What you get is heavy grapefruit, apricot jam, spruce and melons with a big but silky body that lashes your tastebuds out of it with soft bitterness and intense ripe fruit and a mellow roundness from the abv.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22794	/ Galway Bay Gravity’S Rainbow	823	Double IPA	9.0	\N	IN COLLABORATION WITH GALWAY BAY BREWERYGravity's Rainbow combines a grist of Pilsner, Maris Otter, Concerto, Wheat Malt, Torrified Wheat, Flaked Barley and Dextrose (ahem) to produce a nuanced, soft and creamy textured base with which to launch every hop we've got at our disposal into the dirty big can of sesh that is this excercise in excess.100% Whirlpool hopped with Simcoe, fermented on WLP007, then dry hopped every day, for 7 days, with Simcoe, Ekuanot, El Dorado, BRU-1, Citra, Amarillo and Galaxy in that order reaching an eye-watering 32g/L full load before hitting the inside of the can.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22795	Embrace The Daylight	823	Black IPA	6.3	\N	Brewed in collaboration (I sat there and drank tea) with Whiplash to celebrate our 30 years in Stoneybatter floggin' gargle.'Embrace the Daylight' who's name is inspired by a very long night excercising elbows into the brightening early hours of the morning, is a Cascadian dark ale brewed with pale, rye, oat & chocolate malt and hopped up with Columbus, Cascade, Chinook & Centennial.Drink it with shades on !!!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
