25356	Cannonball	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Cannonball is an India Pale Ale in the true tradition, high in alcohol and massively hopped to survive a long sea voyage. We don’ t want you to wait though, crack the cap and let the flavour explode on your palate. Tropically fruity, resinous hops compete against a sweet malty backbone, while a rasping bitterness builds to a mouth puckering crescendo. Our hop bomb might just blow you away…	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25363	Inhaler	5454	Session IPA	4.5	\N	Things move quickly in the beer world and our latest pale ale/IPA hybrid is designed to showcase some of the newer hop varieties which work so well in modern hop forward beers. Pale malt, a little crystal malt,low bitterness and then six different hops! Super fruity, super ripe, super juicy and super drinkable. Breathe it in!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25583	Unsettled	5456	New England IPA	6.2	\N	The haze craze has landed at Central Waters! Expect this Hazy IPA to have a soft mouthfeel with citrus and fruit forward hops reminiscent of orange and guava.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.822564	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25364	Un-Human Cannonball	5454	Double IPA	11.0	\N	Once a year we receive the latest crop of hops from the US, intensely aromatic and bursting with potential they’re begging to be put to work. With three times the quantity of hops of our explosive IPA ‘Cannonball’ and even more than our flagship Double IPA ‘Human Cannonball’ we’ve created a fitting tribute to the new hop release with this our annual homage to the hop. ‘Un-Human Cannonball ‘takes IPA to another dimension balancing massive citric aroma, deep tropical fruit flavor and gravity defying drinkability to deliver a hop experience that is out of this world. We’ve done our best for the hops don’t let them down by aging this beer, please drink as soon as Un-Humanly possible!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25365	Human Cannonball	5454	Double IPA	9.2	\N	Meet Cannonball’s big brother; we used more malt, more hops and more magical conjuring to crank up the flavour of our explosive IPA ‘Cannonball’. Get your taste buds ready for massive pine and candied orange aromas combined with bitter/sweet grapefruit and mango flavours all complemented by a deeply composed, satisfyingly malty base. Ever wondered what it feels like to be shot out of a cannon? Here’s what it tastes like…	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25366	Magic 8 Ball	5454	Black IPA	7.0	\N	Our Black IPA fuses speciality malts with a tropical punch bowl of new world hops to deliver a contradictory yet cultured concoction. A classically ‘pale’ aroma and quenchingly fruity palate belies a broodingly dark and deceptive appearance. Can a beer be both ‘black and pale’? Time to consult the Magic 8 Ball.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25370	Fantasma	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	Gluten free.A dank and juicy IPA using Golden Promise, wheat and Cara Munich malts in the mash for a sweetly smooth body. For the hops we judiciously bittered with Magnum in the kettle followed by Citra T90 in both the whirlpool and in dry-hopping. The aroma/flavour is fruit-filled, dank and resinous, with plenty of tropical mango giving a moreish drinkability. Fermented with our house American ale yeast (WLP001) for a refreshingly clean finish, this IPA is also our first gluten-free beer using Brewers Clarex®.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25373	Hypnotist	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.8	\N	Hazy IPA using Golden Promise, Oats, Rye and acid malt in the mash for a smooth and lightly sour/tart body. Citra, Amarillo, Mosaic and Simcoe T90 hops were used in the whirlpool and Citra, Mosaic & Simcoe Cryo Hops™ Lupulin Powder from Yakima Hop Farms in the dry hop creating big tropical aromas and juicy tart flavour. We used low levels of Coriander seed to contribute geraniol and linalool flavor compounds which augment the fruity and floral character of the hops and yeast. We then fermented with US ‘double IPA yeast’ for a peachy aroma. Deeply fruity, refreshing and drinkable…. are you feeling sleepy yet?	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25375	Simpleton	5454	Session IPA	3.0	\N	A beer lacking in alcohol can’t be really flavourful as well can it? Common sense says it won’t have a big aroma full of passion fruit and mango; it wouldn’t have a well rounded mouth feel and crisp bitterness and there’s no way it’d have satisfying IPA style depth of flavour…. is there? Think again, this is a beer totally devoid of common sense, the jester in the pack, a complete Simpleton…”	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25378	Villainous	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	We’ve wanted to include another IPA in the range for a while so we picked up with an idea that Stu first mentioned back in 2011, an IPA containing 100% Vienna malt. In contrast to what we wanted with Cannonball this would give the beer a bit more body and also a biscuity/toasty flavour to balance the hops against.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25381	The Big Top	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	8.0	\N	An 'India Red Ale'A deeply red, raucously hopped showstopper of a beer. We took our Rapture red hop recipe and turned the volume up to 11. A kaleidoscope of speciality malts deliver a robust yet smoothly sweet mouth feel while sack loads of Australian whole hops bring tropical fruit flavours of lychee, papaya and passion fruit. For the grand finale we introduced waves of magic aroma by dry hopping the beer with kg after kg of those same big and beautifully pungent Aussie hops. Roll up, roll up, The Big Top is in town!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25383	Half Cut	5454	Double IPA	8.0	\N	Draught;Can.A DIPA collaboration with our friends from Brooklyn, Other Half Brewing. Along with our pale malt Golden Promise, the beer uses a reasonably large percentage of oats in the mash for a creamy body and soft mouthfeel.A low bitterness target (for a DIPA) of around 60IBU was aimed for and Citra, Mosaic & Denali hops added to the whirlpool for loads of tropical/citrus flavour. We went heavy on the dry hopping with lots more Citra and Mosaic as well as some Simcoe, Amarillo & HBC 438. The finished beer has a really punchy aroma as well as a super juicy fruit like flavour and soft mouthfeel.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25384	What Are The Odds?	5454	Double IPA	8.3	\N	Collaborative hazy DIPA with Cornish hop wizards Verdant Brew Co. Featuring a high percentage of wheat in the mash to aid haze stability and double dry hopped with Citra, Simcoe, Mosaic and Sabro to aid deliciousness. Fermented with London Fog ale yeast for a big fruity aroma and a juicy finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25388	Cigarro Roja Magica	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	2015 Rainbow project collaboration with Cigar City Brewing of Tampa FL. A fruit filled hop forward IPA brewed in Yorkshire, inspired by the colour red and Floridian sunshine.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25392	Cross Pollination	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.4	\N	Heather Honey IPA brewed in collaboration with Arizona Wilderness Silver Medal, Honey Beer, World Beer Cup 2016.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25393	Neo-Human Cannonball	5454	New England Double IPA	9.2	\N	A New England update on our Double IPA Human Cannonball, this DIPA uses a high percentage of oats and wheat in the grist for a creamy smooth mouthfeel. We eliminated the bittering and moved the majority of whirlpool hops over to the dry hopping to maximise aroma. Fermented with London Fog yeast for an estery aroma and sweet finish the beer is served way more hazy than the original to maximise the flavour expression.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25396	Timequake	5454	Session IPA	4.5	\N	A collaboration with San Diego brew wizards Modern Times, Andrew and Luke joined up with us a few weeks back to create a super sessionable modern style IPA. With this recipe we went heavy on the Rye malt to add body/flavour allied to low bitterness and a high finishing gravity to balance things out. As you might expect this was joined by some very generous hop dosing both in whirlpool and dry hop, using lots of good hops (none of the bad ones) to create this super crushable 4.5% session IPA with a deep hop flavour and spicy finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25425	Zenne-Like	5454	Belgian IPA	6.5	\N	Our good friend Yvan from De La Senne decided to make a trip to Huddersfield, so we brewed a Belgian IPA hitting 6.5%. It features Whole Saphir Leaf and a Bastogne Belgian Ale yeast, giving it an herby, lightly fruity flavour with hints of clove.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25398	Big Dipper	5454	Double IPA	8.3	\N	Double IPA brewed with our friends from over t’hills, Cloudwater Brew Co. Golden Promise, Wheat, Oat and Crystal Malt were used for a smooth, golden, malty body. A combination of Magnum, Citra, Simcoe, Eureka and Mosaic T90 hops were used in the whirlpool and dry hopping, with additional Citra – ‘Cryo Hops™ Lupulin Powder’ added in the dry hop. Fermented with US ‘Double IPA’ yeast, the result is a massively fruit-filled DIPA with loads of Mango and Peach aroma/flavour and gravity-defying drinkability. Strap yourself in!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25399	Telepathy	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.2	\N	Our latest IPA is a development of our recent Demonali IPA recipe, showcasing the new hop varietal Denali. Golden Promise malt was used in addition to Golden Naked Oats, Wheat and Pin Head Oats to achieve a smoother body. We added lots more Denali hops giving the beer big Pineapple and Pine aromatics and added in Citra and Simcoe lupulin powder for more tropical fruit and pine flavours. The beer was fermented with London Ale III for that juicy aroma and long finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25400	Hedonic Escalation	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.7	\N	A tropical IPA using house Golden Promise, Oats and Wheat for body and a little Caramalt for residual sweetness. Judiciously hopped with Simcoe, Ekuanot, HBC 438, Huell Melon and Motueka in whirlpool and dry hop. The hops adding flavours and aromas of passionfruit, melon and lime. Fermented with Brett Trois for a pineapple/mango aroma and a lightly tart and refreshing finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25401	Clairvoyance	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	Our next 500ml can is an IPA brewed with Golden Naked Oats and wheat for a smooth body. We used some acidulated malt to lower PH and dextrose to lighten the body. We omitted the bittering hops as we felt the large hop charge in the whirlpool would add enough bitterness. In a change to the previous 500ml cans we fermented this IPA with our trusty California ale strain with the intention of delivering a more defined hop flavour and aroma and increased drinkability.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25404	Ginspired	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.4	\N	Collaboration with Siren. Gin & Tonic IPA	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25405	Saucery	5454	Session IPA	3.9	\N	A supernatural session IPA made for drinking all day long. Lightly sweet and malty Golden Promise™ malt, a balanced bitterness and layers of tropical fruit filled Citra and Ekuanot hops in whirlpool and dry hop. Fermented with London Ale II yeast to add more fruity body, and enhance malt and hop profile…. Same again?	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25409	Botany Of Desire	5454	Double IPA	8.7	\N	Next up for the big can special treatment is ‘Botany of Desire’ an 8.7% Double IPA, featuring house Golden Promise, Wheat Malt and Pinhead Oats for a creamy hazy body. Hopped at around 18g/l with Mosaic, Citra, Simcoe and Denali which give tropical pineapple, citrus and stone fruit flavours and then fermented with a mixture of WLP644M (Brett Trois) and our house WLP001 (US ale yeast) for a bright tropical aroma and tart finish reminiscent of breakfast juice.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25410	Psychokinesis	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	Our next IPA features new experimental hop HBC438 from YCH. We used a simple Golden Promise malt bill allied to some oats for a clean body and smooth mouthfeel. A small amount of Cascade was used in bittering, with Citra, Simcoe and HBC 438 in whirlpool and Citra, Simcoe HBC 438, and Mosaic in dry hop. An expressive aroma featuring Pineapple, Mango, and Coconut is backed up with a punchy tropical flavour full of stone fruit and lime. The finish is slightly minty/spicy with an herbal bitterness. Unusual, intriguing, fruity and weirdly moreish we’ll leave anymore interpretations of this crazy hop up to you.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25412	Exaltation	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	5.5	\N	A collaborative Session IPA made with our friends at Thornbridge Brewery and brewed with flavour, mouthfeel and drinkability in mind. Malted Rye, Golden Naked Oats and Aromatic Malt were used for body and flavor. Cascade, Amarillo, Simcoe & Centennial hops were chosen for delicious bright citrus and pine aroma and flavor. The beer was fermented with WLP002 (London Ale 2) to accentuate the sweet, full body of the malt and fruit filled character of the hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25415	Wayniac	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.4	\N	A bold and beautiful balanced India Pale Ale brewed with our buddy Wayne from Cigar City Brewing. Golden Promise, Wheat and Crystal Malt in the mash add sweetness and a smooth body. End of Boil/Whirlpool and Dry hop additions of T90 Galaxy, Simcoe, Eureka and Lupulin Powder Mosaic & Citra hops (70kg in total!) make for a tropically fruity aroma and flavour redolent of Mango, Passion Fruit and Citrus. Fermented with US ‘double IPA yeast’ for a big mouthfeel and peachy aroma.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25416	Mind Control	5454	Double IPA	8.0	\N	An 8% double IPA using Golden Promise, Oats and Wheat in the mash for a smooth rounded mouthfeel. Heavily hopped in whirlpool and dry-hop at around 13g/l with Simcoe, Amarillo, CTZ and Mosaic Lupulin powder, de-bittered leaf pellets and LupuLN2 pellets. The hops giving familiar citrus and stone fruit flavours with a slightly dank edge. The beer was fermented with London Ale II, which adds a berry/stone fruit aroma and a slightly sweet finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25418	Grower Owned	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	We were delighted to have Senior VP of Operations of YCH-Hop Union, Karl Vanevenhoven stop by to brew with us in Huddersfield a couple of weeks back. Our production manager Nick has known Karl for a few years now and that connection has allowed us to form a great relationship with YCH. As a brief introduction, YCH Hops is a supplier of hops and hop products in and around the Yakima valley in Oregon, USA. For the most part they keep us supplied with our favourite US hops such as, Citra, Simcoe, Mosaic and Amarillo.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25420	Cryo Baby	5454	Session IPA	4.8	\N	A session IPA collaboration with our friends from CR/AK brewery in Italy. Claudio and Marco joined us a few weeks back to discuss our love of hops and our shared belief in drinkability. With this is mind we brewed a ‘baby’ IPA with a healthy proportion of oats for a baby smooth body and a small quantity of Cascade in bittering. The beer was then hopped in the whirpool and dry hop with Amarillo, Mosaic & Citra Cryo Hops™ Lupulin Powder for mouthfuls of juicy flavour. We then fermented the beer with London Ale III, for a complimentary fruity aroma and moreish finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25428	The Fabulist	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.2	\N	A dank and juicy IPA using Golden Promise, wheat and Cara Munich malts in the mash for a sweetly smooth and hazy body. Bittered lightly with Magnum in the kettle followed by Citra T90 in both the whirlpool and in dry-hopping. We also added T90 Simcoe, Ekuanot, and Mosaic in dry hopping. The aroma/flavour is fruit-filled, dank and resinous, with plenty of tropical mango, passion fruit and pine.Malts: Golden Promise, Wheat, Cara MunichHops: T90 Magnum, Citra, Ekuanot, Mosaic, SimcoeYeast: WLP001 American Ale Yeast	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25434	Damn, Son!	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	A collaboration with Hawkshead Brewery, this fruit adjunct IPA was kettle soured for a bright acidity but also used lactose in the kettle to add body and sweetness. The beer was fermented with a mix of Brett Trois and our house US ale yeast to add a tropical fruity aroma and tart finish. We also used some hibiscus flowers in the hop back to augment the pink colour and add a berry note to the flavour.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25435	Smallvoice	5454	Session IPA	4.3	\N	A collaboration with Dry & Bitter Brewing as part of the ‘Hops not Hate’ initiative. Reflecting our breweries shared love of hops and big drinkability we have progressed our quest further with this low ABV Session IPA. For the mash we used oats, rye and dextrin malt to add body and acidulated malt to aid hop expression. Hop wise Citra, Simcoe, Mosaic and Ekuanot were used in whirlpool and more of the same in dry hop for big tropical hop aroma/flavour. The beer was fermented with super fruity London Ale II yeast for a sweet and juicy finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25436	Fridge Life	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	We found Finback in our fridge, so we decided to make a beer. This DDH IPA is packed with T90 Mosaic, Denali and Simco and is dry hopped with Cryo Hops™, Mosaic and Simcoe.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25437	Yeah Yeah Yeah	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	Dave from Wylam Brewery travelled down from Newcastle and not only came on the daily bread pick up, but also made a beer with us. We have a long-standing friendship with Wylam, so we were happy to finally have them over to brew. Dry hopping it with predominately Loral and a touch of Lemon Drop, this DDH Brut IPA is effortlessly floral, with a dry finish. True to style this beer is dry, crisp and refreshing..Malt: Golden Promise & Maris OtterHops: T90 – Lemon Drop & Mandarina Bavaria / Cryo ™ - Loral & CitraYeast: WLP001	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25438	Craft Magic	5454	Session IPA	3.2	\N	A ’session IPA’ brewed specially for the Craft Beer Co. group London. Cascade and Simcoe whole cone hops in the hop back and dry hopped with Citra and Galaxy in conditioning. Session beer the same but different.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25441	Demonali	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.2	\N	We have an experimental IPA out this week designed to showcase two new hops from Hopsteiner. Demonali is an old school west coast IPA using ‘Denali’ and ‘Lemon Drop’ hops in whirlpool and dry hop.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25442	Micromachine	5454	Session IPA	2.8	\N	A teeny tiny micro IPA, brewed with our pals from just down the road Northern Monk, featuring house Golden Promise and a good proportion of Oats and Wheat for a smooth body. We double dry hopped in fermenter for bags of tropical fruit flavour and fermented with London Fog for a lightly sweet finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25445	Caffeineball Ipa	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	Coffee IPA	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25448	/ Naparbier Modernisme	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	Brewed in collaboration with our friends from Naparbeer. Juan and Beinat from NaparBier joined us a few weeks back to brew this fruity and refreshing IPA full of Spanish sunshine. The beer has loads of Mango and Apricot in the aroma/flavour with a smooth body, subtle bitterness and great drinkability. In case you’re wondering about the name, ‘Modernisme’ also known as ‘Catalan modernism’, is the historiographic denomination given to an art, literature (and now beer?) movement.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25450	Brother Chucker	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.7	\N	A collaboration with our mates at Basqueland Brewing Project, brewed to remind us of a fun filled week of bikes, beer, baked cheesecake, big smiles and err…. darts in the Basque country. A smooth malt bill featuring Golden Promise, wheat and golden naked oats, alongside a defined bitterness to aid drinkability. We then used lots of lovely piney/citrus Simcoe and limey New Zealand Motueka hops as well as a dash of tropically crazy HBC 438.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25569	Rift	5456	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	Over five breeds of heron have made their home in the Great Rift Valley region of Kenya. Likewise, we have taken their lead by crafting an IPA with five different hops blanketed over a foundation of clean malt. Featuring Simcoe, Citra, & Amarillo hops this is our take on the American IPA.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.822564	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25454	Beauregarde	5454	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.0	\N	Our beer for the inaugural ‘Rainbow IPA challenge 2013’. Made with a pale golden promise malt base, and our house yeast, we then used litre after litre of pure Blueberries in fermentation and dry hopped the beer with berry like Vanguard/Willamette and citrusy Chinook hops.  A deep red colour with an inviting off white head, the flavor is full of characteristic blueberry fruit with a crisp and drying berry skin finish. Don’t end up like Violet!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25456	Ink & Dagger	5455	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	Modern day IPACan you taste that hop oil slithering down the back of your throat? Can you smell that intense lupulin blast from the bottom of your glass? We turned the volume up to 10 and broke the speaker, our loudest beer buried in a mound of hoppy goodness. Think wet tropical grass, pineapple and mango freshness all crammed into this self-proclaimed hop bomb.Ink & Dagger pairs best with long sessions at the local tattoo parlor.Ingredients: Water, barley malt (Pilsner), hops (Magnum, Citra, Mosaic, Simcoe), yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25457	Apocalyptic Thunder Juice	5455	New England IPA	6.5	\N	New England IPAApocalyptic Thunder Juice is made to be enjoyed as the last beer you will ever have. A celebration to the end of time. The one you have waited your whole life for. We bring praise to the New England style of IPA in the race for the freshest IPA. We bring you our version, cloudy, dank and juicy. It will make you feel alive as the world is crashing down around you.Grab a seat, watch the world burn and listen to 'REM - It's the end of the world as we know it'.Ingredients: water, Pilsener malt, flaked oats, lactose, Mosaic hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25458	Hopbliminal Messages	5455	New England IPA	5.3	\N	New England IPA. Can you imagine going into a hop trance? Imagine yourself drifting on a calm and beautiful river of Lupulin. Picture your muscles becoming loose and limp and your mind being filled by hoppy thoughts. See yourself feeling completely relaxed, enjoying a can of tranced up hop juice.Hopbliminal Messages pairs best with your drinking hand.MALT: Pilsner, Flaked Oats, Wheat​HOPS: Magnum, Mosaic, Simcoe, Citra​YEAST: Vermont Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25459	Oceans Ipa	5455	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.6	\N	Lost adrift on the vast ocean, a team of Amundsen's explorers had a salt water induced fever dream. They dreamt of a powerfully balanced IPA with tropical, piney, hop flavors, dripping with malt sustenance. With their last remaining energy they carved the recipe into the deck of their raft. The last one who survived would make this IPA as a dedication to his lost brothers at sea. What you are holding in your hands is that beer. Meticulously reproduced by Timothy Albert, the lone survivor of the Great Hoptipus Attack of 1897.Ingredients: Water, barley malt (Pilsner, Carared, Caraaroma), hops (Centennial, Columbus, Simcoe, Citra, Cascade), yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25460	Hoptropolis Double Ipa	5455	Double IPA	9.0	\N	So, who actually started this? Who planted the first seed and did they ever imagine a once-bustling metropolis overgrown by their own creation? Controlled hop fields now but a distant memory. The hop vines are trying to overpower and show their dominance in the food chain. The only way to fight back is to brew more beer that contains more hops. This is us doing our part to save humanity. A double dry hopped DIPA, jam packed with massive amounts of lupulin. Bitter, sticky hop love, hitting you in the face with a slap of dankness.Ingredients: Water, barley malt (Pilsner), wheat malt, flaked oats, hops (Magnum, Mosaic, Ekuanot), Vermont yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25461	Everyday Hero	5455	Session IPA	4.7	\N	NEW WORLD IPA.Our city was under attack. Bland, tasteless, mass-produced lager infiltrating every supermarket shelf. Then shone a ray of light: Everyday Hero swooped in to save his hometown. Combining drinkability with a balanced attack of citrus, floral hops and a solid honey malt backbone. No longer will our town be subjected to flavourless conglomerates, thanks to Everyday Hero. Let Everyday Hero save your everyday. MALTPilsner​ HOPS: Magnum, Amarillo, Citra​ YEAST: American Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25462	Lorita	5455	Session IPA	4.7	\N	The esteemed explorer Van Vuuren is an integral part of the Amundsen team. So much so, that we named this beer after his parrot. The intrepid explorer found the recipe for Lorita in a glass bottle along the coast of the Summer Isles. it was said to be a recipe for happiness. The Amundsen team recreated it as best as we could using passion fruit, the rare and esteemed Azacca hop and malted barley. The result is a fruity beer with tropical, refreshing character. We recommend pairing Lorita with a journey on a raft in the South Seas.MALT: Pilsner​HOPS: Cascade, Azacca​YEAST: American Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25577	Caught In The Rain Ipa	5456	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.0	\N	An American IPA brewed with a boatload of fresh pineapple and toasted coconut.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.822564	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25463	Chuggernaut	5455	New England IPA	4.7	\N	New England IPA.On a recent exploration trip to the southern most tip of Africa we met up with the like minded guys at Devil's Peak Brewing Co, and immediately decided to make a beer together. Chuggernaut is a reincarnation of both our flagship beers moulded into one, so chuggable it will blow your mind with a total hop overload, tropical, juicy and hazy. Chuggernaut pairs best with sun, shades and lazy days.MALT: Pilsner, Flaked Oats, Wheat​HOPS: Magnum, Amarillo, Citra, Mosaic​YEAST: Vermont Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25466	Space Tiger	5455	Double IPA	8.5	\N	DDH DIPA.Another day, another collab. This time we teamed up with our good friends from Verdant Brewing Co. Since we both share a huge passion for hoppy beers, we couldn't help but to make one. This double dry hopped double IPA is loaded with a generous 25g/litre dryhop, cramming it full with all the awesome hoppy goodness we all love so much. Tropical, dank & juicy!Space Tiger is best enjoyed on a magic carpet exploring new universes.MALT: Pilsner, Oats, Wheat, Carapils​HOPS: Magnum, Simcoe, Mosaic, Amarillo, Citra, Galaxy​YEAST: London Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25468	Hop Magic	5455	New England IPA	7.0	\N	Collaborations is our happy place, a place to have fun, explore, push boundries and most of all spend a day with some industry friends. In this case we decided to mate it a three-way, Amundsen, Dugges and Dry & Bitter all coming together to create some magic. In this beer we collaborate all our styles to create the ultimate crusher - a tropical, juice hop head butt!!Ingredients: Water, barley malt (Pilsner), wheat malt, flaked oats, lactose, hops (Magnum, Mosaic, Galaxy, Nelson Sauvin, Ekuanot, Citra, Simcoe) Vermont yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25473	Double Apocalypse	5455	Double IPA	8.5	\N	DDH DIPA.Double Apocalypse is a bumped up version of our Apocalyptic Thunder Juice. Everything we love in a beer, dialed up to 11! Made to be enjoyed as the last beer you will ever have. A celebration to the end of time. The one you have waited your whole life for. We bring praise to the New England style IPA and present you with our version - cloudy, dank and juicy. It will make you feel alive as the world crashing down around you.MALT: Pilsner, Flaked Oats, Wheat, Carapils, Lactose​HOPS: Magnum, Mosaic​YEAST: Burlington Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25474	Luponic Plague	5455	New England IPA	7.0	\N	UP HIGH IN THE DARK SKIES, THERE IS A GREEN PLANET WHERE DIFFERENT LIFE FORMS ARE WORKING TOGETHER TO END THE HUMAN RACE. ON THE GREEN PLANET HOPS GROW FREE AND LIVE SIDE BY SIDE IN THEIR BUSTLING HOPTROPOLIS, WITH ALIENS CALLED REPTILIODS. THE REPTILOIDS HAVE BEEN SENDING HOPBLIMINAL MESSAGES TO THE HOP VINES FOR YEARS. THESE MESSAGES ARE PERSUADING THEM TO PRODUCE LUPULIN ON DEMAND. IN TURN THE ALIENS WANTS TO USE THIS LUPULIN TO CREATE THE ULTIMATE LUPONIC PLAGUE. THIS PLAGUE IS DESTINED FOR PLANET EARTH, WHERE THEY WANT TO BRING THE HUMAN RACE TO THEIR KNEES BY INFECTING EACH AND EVERY HOP HEAD WITH COPIOUS AMOUNTS OF HOP JUICE. THE ALIENS KNEW WE WOULD BE WEARY AND DECIDED TO BREW THE ULTIMATE HOPPY BEER WHICH THEY COULD INFECT WITH THEIR PLAGUE. ONCE YOU CRACK OPEN THIS CAN THE AIR WILL BE FILLED WITH A TROPICAL JUICY AROMA, A HOP ENDUCED FEVER SETS IN AND BEGS YOU TO TAKE YOUR FIRST SIP. THIS IS OUR MOST HEAVILY HOPPED BEER TO DATE. HOP LOVE IN A CAN, FROM A HOP LOVING BREWERY...TO YOU!Hops: Magnum, Mosaic, Simcoe, CitraNew England IPA	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25475	Pineapple Oceans	5455	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.6	\N	West Coast Pineapple IPA.The pineapple has long been a symbol of hospitality in the americas, a sign of ships returning home from the caribbean. Amundsen would like to wish you welcome aboard our schooner, the pineapple express. The destination is unknown, but the journey is full of new flavor experiences. You will discover pineapple aromas, intermingling with the american hop forward tropical mango notes of our flagship Oceans IPA. Sit back and relax and let the tropical trade winds catch your sails. Pineapple Oceans pairs best with a handlebar mustache and hawaiian shirt.MALT: Pilsner, Carared, Caraaroma​HOPS: Centennial, Columbus, Citra, Simcoe, Cascade​YEAST: American Ale	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25476	Luponic Plague 2.0	5455	New England IPA	7.0	\N	Up high in the dark skies, there is a green planet where different life forms are working together to end the human race. On the green planet hops grow free and live side by side in their bustling hoptropolis, with aliens called reptiliods. The reptiloids have been sending hopbliminal messages to the hop vines for years. These messages are persuading them to produce lupulin on demand. In turn the aliens wants to use this lupulin to create the ultimate luponic plague. This plague is destined for planet earth, where they want to bring the human race to their knees by infecting each and every hop head with copious amounts of hop juice. The aliens knew we would be weary and decided to brew the ultimate hoppy beer which they could infect with their plague. Once you crack open this can the air will be filled with a tropical juicy aroma, a hop enduced fever sets in and begs you to take your first sip. This is our most heavily hopped beer to date. Hop love in a can, from a hop loving brewery...to you! Luponic plague pairs best with a hop head and lover of the hazy juice.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
