26114	/ Against The Grain Overcompensation	5462	Double IPA	9.0	\N	(Green Can is Upland's Version).  Overcompensation is a collaboration brew with our friends from Against the Grain Brewery out of Louisville, KY. We each brewed and canned our own version of this Double IPA, and we have no doubt you'll find our is hella hoppier than theirs. Five hop varieties—Warrior, Galaxy, El Dorado, Equinot, and experimental BRU-1, plus hops extract for added bittering—give this beer dizzying amounts of tropical fruit and citrus flavors followed by a piney finish. And if the barrage of melon, lime, orange, passion fruit, and papaya aromas wasn’t extravagant enough, Upland brewers added essential oil derived from El Dorado hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
26116	/ Cigar City Galaxy Grove	5462	India Pale Ale (IPA)	7.3	\N	This collaboration with our friends at Cigar City Brewing in Tafmpa, FL is a funky IPA with miles of depth.  During primary fermentation, we use two strains of Brettanomyces, both known for their fruity, tropical characteristics to complement the use of hos.  The beer was then transferred into previously used oak barrels from Upland's  Wood Shop to add a light acidity to the beer before aging on peaches and guavas.  After going through another fermentation on the fruit, the beer was generously dry-hopped with Centennial, Citra, and Galaxy hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
