26268	Nebula Belgian Black Double Ipa	905	Black IPA	8.2	\N	A Belgian, a hophead, an alcoholic, and a sous chef walk into a bar . . .  Sound like a joke?  Well our beer is the punch line.  Belgians are noted for their creative beers with complex flavor profiles that balance flavors from yeast, hops, malt, alcohol, and other flavors.  Nebula taps this creative energy and puts a lot of twists on the traditional IPA.An American IPA has a lot of hops and showcases them often to the degree that most else is buried in the hops flavors.  Not Nebula. With over 70 IBUs, one would expect a bitter hoppy beer, but Nebula balances the hops with the complexity of the darker malts, alcohol and esters, and a Belgian yeast that loves this cocktail. Leave your expectations behind as you enjoy this blend of six sweet malts, four flavorful hops, and complexities that the Belgian monks would appreciate.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
26284	Ganassa	906	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.5	\N	Le imprescindibili. Birra viva non filtrata e non pastorizzata. L’arroganza del luppolo. L’utilizzo di soli malti chiari dona a questa birra un colore giallo paglierino. Dal cappello di schiuma emergono intense note di resina, agrumi e frutta tropicale. In bocca è esplosiva con un finale secco e amaro. Fatevi travolgere dalla Ganassa. Si consiglia di non invecchiare. Servire a 6 - 8° C Ingredienti: acqua, malto d’orzo, luppolo, lievito. Fonzie say Hey! The indispensable. Unleavened and unpasteurized live beer. Honey arrogance. Only light malting gives this beer a straw yellow color. From the foam hat emerge intense notes of resin, citrus fruit and tropical fruit. In the mouth is explosive with a dry and bitter finish. Make yourself overwhelmed by Ganassa. It is advisable not to age. Serve at 6 - 8° C Ingredients: water, barley malt, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
26285	? American Indian Pale Ale	906	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.4	\N	One shot o prototipo? Punto di domanda… La nostra interpretazione di uno degli stili più inflazionati del mondo craft, le American IPA. Si presenta di colore dorato e con una buona frizzantezza, al naso esplosiva grazie all’intensa luppolatura con Columbus, Citra e Sorachi Ace impiegati anche in dry hopping. Tutta la bevuta è dominata dai profumi agrumati e di frutta tropicale del luppolo e un amaro finale che non vi lascerà mai sazi. Servire a 6 - 8° C. Contiene glutine. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d’orzo, luppolo, lievito. 14.1° Plato. One shot of a prototype? Question mark ... Our interpretation of one of the most inflatable styles of craft world, American IPA. It is golden in color and with good sparkiness, explosive nose due to intense hopping with Columbus, Citra and Sorachi Ace also used in dry hopping. Whole drink is dominated by the citrus fruit and tropical fruit of the hop and a bitter finish that will never let you satiate. Serve at 6 - 8° C. Contains gluten. Ingredients: water, barley malt, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
