28485	Wasda #8	5487	India Pale Ale (IPA)	6.2	\N	A Belgian IPA before the holidays? Yes, please!Wadesda is our ‘freedom label’ when we want to try out something new. It can be anything and its opposite, sour, bitter, … This time we had a new hop to test!WADESDA #8 (6,2% abv) is amber with orange reflections, intense fruity flavours of peach, orange, apricots and melon, and tropical floral notes. A light sulphur note structures it and gives it character. Its bitterness is fine and thirst-quenching, and her texture is almost silky.Only available in kegs and in very small amounts. You’ll be able to taste it very soon in many nice bars, the upcoming weekend at Vini Birre Ribelli, and on 2-3 December at Billie’s Craft Beer Fest in Antwerp!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
