13201	Uso Vienna	540	Vienna Lager	5.9	\N	Lager ambrata in stile Vienna non pastorizzata. Birra a bassa fermentazione, di colore ambrato, deve il suo nome allo storico malto utilizzato, che dona particolari note biscottate e appena caramellate, che si sposano con le decise note fruttate e floreali del nuovo luppolo Mandarina Bavaria. ll risultato è di grande intensità, ma anche di grande equilibrio, per una birra che maschera molto bene il grado alcolico e la complessità, mantenendosi pericolosamente beverina. Il suo equilibrio la rende perfetta per una (lunga) serata tra amici, ma la sua parte maltata può bilanciare altrettanto bene la sapidità di alcuni cibi, mentre la profondità della birra rende possibile l'abbinamento anche con piatti di buona intensità. Servire a 8° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo, luppolo, zucchero in rifermentazione, lievito. Amber-colored lager in unpasteurized Vienna style. Low fermentation beer, amber colored, owes its name to the historical malt used, which gives particular of biscuit and just caramelized notes, which are combined with the strong fruity and floral notes of the new hops Mandarina Bavaria. The result is of great intensity, but also of great balance, for a beer that masks the alcohol and the complexity very well, remaining dangerously drinkable. Its balance makes it perfect for a (long) evening with friends, but its malty part can balance the flavor of some foods, while the depth of beer makes it possible to combine it with dishes of good intensity. Serve at 8° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, hops, refermentation sugar, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13269	/ Az Wilderness / Creature Comforts Collaboration No. 7 Oak-Aged Lager	5310	Lager	6.0	\N	For our first collaboration featuring three breweries, we selected our partners following the same approach we?ve used for previous collaboration projects. Our goal is to work with brewers for whom we have mutual respect while learning new techniques and celebrating the strengths of each brewery. Arizona Wilderness has become known as champions for local ingredients in innovative beers while the Creature Comforts crew is ?dedicated to better being through being curious.? It?s no coincidence that we absolutely LOVE enjoying beers with both brewery teams. For the full backstory on our relationships with both breweries, please head to a previous Brewer?s Blog post.Built on a base of two-row pale malt, Sonoran White Wheat, honey malt and corn grits, Collaboration No. 7 ? Oak-Aged Lager showcases Riesling grape juice, peaches and lemon zest in a crisp lager hopped with Nelson Sauvin, Lemondrop and Hallertau Blancs. Following fermentation with the Ayinger lager strain, Collaboration No. 7 was briefly aged on Cuvee No. 5 Tank Staves, French oak staves that impart fruit, spice, toast and tannins similar to aging in a fresh/virgin French oak barrel.At 6% ABV and 16 IBUs, Collaboration No. 7 Oak-Aged Lager pours a brilliant golden color with tight, off-white lacing. Bright aromas of peach and Riesling grapes mingle with the tropical fruit notes provided by subtle hopping. Lemon zest accentuates the naturally citrusy character of the beer as the malt bill forms a slightly sweet, honey-like base from which the chosen regional ingredients shine. French oak character lends a drying effect resulting in a bright, fruity lager that finishes incredibly crisp. Bottle conditioned with champagne yeast, Collaboration No. 7 ? Oak-Aged Lager has fluffy, effervescent carbonation that scrubs the palate and begs for another sip.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13427	Birreros Tipo C	546	India Pale Lager	5.4	\N	Birra senza glutine, non filtrata e non pastorizzata, prodotta in modo naturale senza aggiunta di coloranti o conservanti. La leggera torbidità ed eventuali sedimenti di lievito sul fondo della bottiglia sono caratteristiche della genuinità della birra. Temperatura di servizio 10 - 12° C. Prodotto e imbottigliato nel laboratorio artigiano di Ghislenghien (Belgium). Ingredienti: acqua, malto d’orzo, riso, luppolo.Gluten-free beer, unfiltered and unpasteurized, produced in a natural way to operate with no added colors or preservatives. The slight turbidity and any yeast sediment on the bottom of the bottle are features of the purity of beer. Serving temperature 10 - 12° C. Produced and bottled in the craft workshop of Ghislenghien (Belgium). Ingredients: water, barley malt, rice, hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
