23825	I Got Pils, Now What?	5439	India Pale Lager	5.7	\N	When Paul came to visit we naturallywent to the bar, where he drank oneof our pilsners, which led him to askif we could brew up a collab pilsnerin addition to the IPA we alreadyintended to brew together… so ofcourse we agreed. We love a greatpilsner and feel that pilsner is toooften demonized in the craft beercommunity, so this would be the bestway to showcase what pilsner candeliver. Light and easy, yet hoppedwith European only varietals, we wentthrough the choices we have in the hopfridge and found a few that would beperfect. We took the fruity, citruscharacter of Mandarina Bavaria andthe peachy passion fruit notes ofGrüngeist, and punched it UP withfloral, lemony Perle hops. Then, forgood measure, we did it twice againin the dry hopping.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.124448	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1574216364975-51fcb7fffd8e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
