653	Speedway Stout - Double Hammerhead	5186	Imperial Stout	12.0	\N	Served at SDBW 2014, Speedway Grand Prix. Served at Copenhagen Beer Celebration 2015.Speedway Stout with cracked African and Sumatran coffee beans plus fresh espresso. This version has double the coffee from regular Hammerhead.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-21 23:19:11.573064	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
654	Speedway Stout - Boxcar	5186	Imperial Stout	13.0	\N	Imperial Stout with Cacao Nibs, Vanilla Beans, Chili Peppers & Coffee All Aged in Premium Bourbon Barrels.To celebrate a decade of serving up San Diego Craft Beer, we decided to create an extremely special beer in collaboration with the brewery that kicked off our love of homebrewing, and that has been a major part of our history from day one -- AleSmith Brewing Company. After brainstorming with Peter Zien we decided on a Barrel-Aged Speedway variation that would add layers, depths, complexity, and a little heat to this already unique beer. This beer is the collaborative effort of elite brewers, judges, roasters, and passionate industry compatriots. The name BOXCAR came second and is a nod to the old railcars, whose tracks cut around the AleSmith brewery.The Coffee:  Swell Coffee Co supplied us with a custom blend of ultra-premium Colombian and Burundian coffees designed to hold up to the strength of this beer while imparting their own nuanced flavor characteristics. 25% Peaberry grade coffee from Kayanza, Burundi in Africa. Peaberry grade coffee is produced from a natural mutation of the bean inside the cherry, where only a single beer is present inside the cherry providing a denser, sweeter and more flavoured coffee. Tasting Notes: Peach and butterscotch75% Finca la Virgen de Oro from Antioquia, Colombia, this is a true estate coffee, meaning its beans are milled an packed at the farm, unlike any other Colombian coffee.Tasting Notes: Strawberry, floral, sweet pepper and molassesThe Chiles: We used a blend of Hatch and mulatto chiles to further add to the complexity of the beer while contributing a touch of back end heat. The Hatch chiles provide sweet earthiness, while the mulatto chiles contribute notes of chocolate, cherry and tobacco.Cacao nibs and vanilla beans:Boxcar was also aged on Brazilian Forestero cacoa nibs and a healthy dose of Bourbon Madagascar vanilla beans, which accentuate the sweeter, complex whiskey character of this beer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-21 23:19:11.79724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
