11152	Sticky Toffee Strannik	5288	Imperial Stout	10.0	\N	We took our deeply roasted signature Russian imperial stout, Strannik, and we added golden syrup and Demerera sugar to ramp up those sticky toffee vibes. Hitting those rich, warming dessert notes, it's an ideal companion for those cold, dark winter evenings we are oh so familiar with.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11157	Patrons Project 2.06 Nowt Like A Proper	5288	Stout	7.3	\N	2.06 KENTUCKYSHIRE BREAKFAST STOUT // NOMAD CLAN // NOWT LIKE A PROPER BREW // AGAINST THE GRAIN. When looking to brew with our good friends from Against the Grain, we looked to brew an American classic but with a decidedly Yorkshire twist; and like our previous collaborations together, with a touch of Southern hospitality! The result? This delicious Anglo-American inspired stout!We drew inspiration from everyone’s favourite welcome to the day; breakfast! We like it hearty with a good stack of pancakes, smoky bacon and maple syrup to kick start the day the proper way!Using a portion of smoked wheat to get the taste buds salivating, healthy additions of strong coffee to get us going and maple to add a sweet finish to send us off about our business; this beer is just as good later in the day to keep the party going.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11162	Patrons Project 14.02 Monocromicon	5288	Imperial Stout	10.0	\N	After hanging out at Dark City last year we simply had to make a beer with our good friends at Amundsen! We were all blown away by their big, flavourful beers and they were many of the staff’s beers of the festival. With masses of flavour packed into the beer, it’s hard not to be completely taken with their imperial stouts; we knew straight away that this was the style of beer we were out to make!Using nine different malts, three different FV additions and two different sugars, we wanted to make a beer with massive layers of flavour and a depth that couldn’t be ignored; using the adjuncts to intensify the flavours within rather than mask them. Additions of cherry, muscovado, cocoa, tonka bean help boost the natural dark malt flavours and complete this big beast of a beer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1572490122747-3968b75cc699?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
