11623	Collab 04 Lost Abbey Sticks N' S	5292	Imperial Pilsner	8.3	\N	Before the meaning of the name is revealed for that “ah-ha” moment, we must elaborate on the significance of the collaboration. Three key Stone brewers gathered together with long-time friend and Lost Abbey brewmaster Tomme Arthur in Berlin. There they collaborated on a beer representative of our presence in Germany and the craft beer crusade we have been on and never lost sight of despite all of the words of criticism. Too aggressive, too many hops, too expensive, too impossible to break into centuries of German tradition…all of that was just words. It didn’t break us. And here we are, two decades later with a foothold in Berlin and our fingertips on the international craft beer moment. In honor of that we brewed a dark imperial lager with a German yeast strain and partially aged it with wooden chips “sticks” in stone granite barrels. Ah-ha.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.944228	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566919317267-b5e1b2bb2b15?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566919317267-b5e1b2bb2b15?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
