19355	Biren The Geese Suite Beer	720	Pilsner	5.2	\N	The Anthony Phillips 40th Anniversary Beer Series. After having been a primary force of Genesis from 1967 to 1970 - and recording two albums with them, From Genesis To Revelation and Trespass - Anthony Phillips spent some six years developing his music skills as well as composing and recording the music for his debut album called The Geese And The Ghost, a marvellous piece of art that thrilled - thanks also to its magical illustrations by Peter Cross - not only Genesis fandom but the whole Progressive rock world. The Geese Suite Beer - a craft beer - celebrates the 40th anniversary of The Geese And The Ghost’s release. So pop it and taste it whilst listening to Ant’s masterpiece, in good company if possible. And then put the bottle on the shelf beside your favorite records, because with this label it’s also an item to collect. Andrea C. Soncini. We love good music. And we love its best companion: a good craft beer. Artwork/Images copyright of Peter Cross & Anthony Phillips. All rights reserved. Ingredients: water, barley malt, hop, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.608724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566919317267-b5e1b2bb2b15?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1566919317267-b5e1b2bb2b15?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
