741	Haantjesbier	140	Traditional Ale	8.3	\N	This beer is based on a historical recipe from the 1860s. Originally made for export to the colonies, it was a heavy beer aged in barrels for months and had Brandy and Juniper Berries added. We adjusted the recipe in negotiation with beer historian Roel Mulder. We fermented on stainless and used Brandy soaked juniper berries and added a Brett culture (as this pre-pasteur beer would probably have it), letting it ferment and age for half a year.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-21 23:19:31.736777	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
742	/ Siren The Crooked Nykk	140	Traditional Ale	8.5	\N	Imagine yourself walking through a flower garden in the mythical Norwegian lands and you hear a mysterious honey-voiced song. That's where you'll see it: The CROOKED NYKK!When we finally set a date to brew with Steve Hoile from Siren Craft Brew, we knew the brew was going to be unique. We’ve delved into the world of kveik, traditional yeast cultures traditionally used in Norway. These beers are unlike what we have ever tasted, with big, bold flowery and fruity flavours. We added honey and zest to let these flavours shine.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-21 23:19:31.962075	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
745	First Strong Ale	141	Golden Ale / Blond Ale	6.3	\N	Birra calda e morbida con un corpo rotondo adatto a riscaldare tutti i cuori. Prodotto artigianale non pastorizzato e non microfiltrato. I lieviti sul fondo sono una caratteristica naturale del prodotto. Abbinamenti: pesci, crostacei e carni bianche. Colore biondo opaco. Sapore agrumato. Temperatura di servizio 7 - 9° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d’orzo, malto di frumento, luppolo, lievito.Warm and soft beer with a round body suitable to warm every heart. Handmade product unpasteurized and not micro-filtered. The yeasts on the bottom are a natural characteristic of the product. Serving suggestions: fish, shellfish and white meats. matte blonde color. citrusy flavor. Serving temperature 7 - 9° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, wheat malt, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-21 23:19:32.637872	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
