4586	La Trippale	5228	Belgian Strong Ale	8.5	\N	Cask, keg & bottle conditioned; Special.Note: Bottled version brewed at Bristol Beer Factory.A New World Tripel collaboration between Bristol Beer Factory, Arbor and Harbour breweries.A marriage of American and Belgian brewing techniques, using a special strain of Belgian yeast and brewed using traditional open-top fermenters, this beer has a distinct dryness with a peppery, spicy finish and a big hoppy twist. An Imperial IPA malt bill, powerfully hopped and conditioned with Nugget, Summit and Amarillo.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
4592	Single Hop Lubelski	5228	Golden Ale / Blond Ale	4.0	\N	Cask & nottle conditioned; Occasional.Originally a cask special in July 2009. Reappeared (in bottle at least) in 2012.As the name suggests, we’ve used just one variety of hop in this pale golden ale. Brewed with just low colour Maris Otter malt and a little wheat for head retention, we’ve selected some of the more “interesting” hops that we haven’t used before and added several bucket loads to each brew. The first brew is made with the Polish hop “Lubelski”, a very noble hop indeed. Expect a beer that’s not too bitter with plenty of spicy notes.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.288158	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
