5249	Groen	276	Sour / Wild Ale	5.0	\N	This wild ale is dryhopped with a vast amount of mostly noble German hops. Groen needed 6 months in the bottle to balance out all the flavours and bitterness. It's really interesting to see how the hop aroma's stay and change in the bottle over time in a good way. The beer has notes of lemons, herbs and a kind of farmhouse yeast character.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.485546	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
5250	Braam-Vlier	276	Sour / Wild Ale	5.0	\N	\N	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.485546	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
5251	Lieve	276	Sour / Wild Ale	5.0	\N	A wild ale refermented with organic Chardonnay grapes. A hybrid of a farmhouse cider, natural white wine and beer. It has an intense aroma and strong tannins, because of the long maturation of the grapes. Complex flavour and wild yeast notes. I would recommend to decant the beer to let the aromas open up to their full potential.Ingredients: water, organic malted barley, organic wheat, organic hops, organic grapes (Chardonnay), wild yeast and lactic acid bacteria.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.485546	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
5252	Liefste	276	Sour / Wild Ale	5.0	\N	A wild ale refermented with chardonnay grapes. It is a more elegant version of Lieve. It has a wine-like character with notes of cider and a touch of oak. The complexity of the winegrapes and the funk will complement the lightness of the overall beer.We recommend to drink this beer either fresh, or aged if you prefer more funk and a rounder flavor.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:41.485546	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
