7276	Garage Service	5250	Sour / Wild Ale	6.2	\N	Brewed exclusively for Toronado SF 30th Anniversary. Served with a side of grit, Garage Service is a blend of gold and red sour beers aged in oak barrels with plums and prickly pear that drives notes of candied plums, dried berries, and orange peel. The name comes from the iconic neon that hangs above the bar. Originally th sign was attached to the Manx Hotel which opened in 1909 on Powell St at O’Farrel (it is now the Villa Florence). In the early 90’s a Toronado regular, Andrew Franklin, who was working on the hotel renovation saved the garage service sign from being thrown away and gave it to Dave.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.22296	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
