7290	Dubious Dawn	5250	Sour / Wild Ale	5.8	\N	Dark sour ale aged in oak tequila barrels with apricots.Dubious Dawn is our fourth release in the Dubious Series. What’s that? Well, it all starts with being open to letting the creative juices flow. Often, the barrels that we’re tasting are created with the intent of being blended to make a specific beer. However, as our team tastes through barrels, a metaphorical light bulb will switch on, and we’ll come up with a blend that combines a variety of barrels that we didn’t originally intend on blending. Ideas that may appear as suspect when proposed, can often surprise us in reality. The barrels speak, and we listen. At its core, the Dubious Series is simply another way for us to encourage creativity throughout the blending process.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.22296	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
7291	Mister Tea	5250	Sour / Wild Ale	6.3	\N	Mister Tea is a blend of golden sour beers aged in oak barrels with Jade Needle white tea. This 2 oak barrel blend was infused with a little over 4 and a half pounds of tea for over an hour, however, the notes derived from the tea are quite restrained and blend in with the base beer seamlessly. Showcasing aromas of jasmine and hay with fruity notes of peach and mandarin, Mister Tea is easy drinking.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.22296	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
