8191	Daylight Amber	5257	Amber Ale	6.3	\N	Don’t be fooled by Daylight Amber’s easy going name. It is a bit more aggressive than the name implies. Daylight Amber has the upfront bitterness of an IPA, but that bitterness fades into a malt body influenced by caramel and toasted flavors, which are more typical of an Amber Ale. Too firmly hopped to be a pure Amber and too malty to be a considered an IPA, Daylight Amber represents the best of both worlds.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.622897	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
8193	Bee Line Blonde	5257	Golden Ale / Blond Ale	5.3	\N	When Track 7 Brewing Co. first launched, the Bee Line Blonde was not originally anticipated to be one of the regular beers included as part of our regular line-up.  However, we received an overwhelmingly positive response from the initial trial batches, so we brewed our first full batch on 1/29/12.  Bee Line Blonde is a Honey Blonde Ale that incorporates European continental hops and a generous amount of Sacramento-area wildflower honey.  The result is a delicate ale with hints of flowers on the nose and a subtle spice on the pallet.  This ale makes a wonderful compliment to our other hoppier offerings, so make a bee line down to Track 7 and acquaint yourself with our newest offering.Hops: Fuggle, Magnum, Tettnang	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:42.622897	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
