11205	Verde	481	Golden Ale / Blond Ale	4.5	\N	Un tono di amaro deciso ma non invadente Note agrumate e leggermente speziate fanno di lei una birra fresca e rotonda. La schiuma fine dal colore bianco le conferisce eleganza e la protegge dall’ossidazione.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11207	Gouden Carolus Classic	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	8.5	\N	Het Anker Brewery still brews 'The Emperor’s Beer' which is top-fermented and bottle conditioned following traditional methods. Its high gravity (O.G. 1080-85) combines the warmth of wine and the freshness of beer. Gouden Carolus is one of the strongest and most exciting beers in the world. After lengthy maturing and conditioning, it is bottled unfiltered, giving a beer which is rich in vitamins and 100% natural. Gouden Carolus has unlimited storage (it even improves with age) and will charm you with its warm coppery colour and rich bouquet.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11332	Cerveja Letra / Boxing Cat Missionary Ale	487	Pale Ale	5.0	\N	Brewed with Boxing Cat (Shanghai, China). Pale ale with green tea Lung Ching and lemon peel.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11208	Gouden Carolus Christmas/Noël	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	10.5	\N	For more than 35 years we had to miss the Christmas beer but in 2002 the tradition was restored with Gouden Carolus Christmas. It’s a strong, dark ruby red ale with character and contains an alcohol percentage of 10.5 % alc.vol. Brewed in August, the beer rests a few months to reach an optimal balance. Six different kinds of herbs and spices and three different kinds of hops define the rich taste followed by a long, well-seasoned aftertaste. Perfect combination with wild, stews or ripened, strong cheeses. Top-class!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11210	Gouden Carolus Hopsinjoor	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	8.0	\N	Bottle: UnfilteredOrigin: Gouden Carolus Hopsinjoor completes the taste pallet of the gamma Carolus-beers.Name: 'Hopsinjoor' is a wordplay to for one thing the several hops which were used, and on the other hand the typical character of Mechelen of Gouden Carolus: the figure 'opsinjoor' is intertwined with the history of Mechelen (see: www.opsinjoorke.be/Opsinjoorke/opsinjoor.htm).5 types of hops are used in this beer. These hops were fractioned at several times in the cooking process in order to keep a maximum of aroma.Regarding to taste we can say that the beer has a gentle, but nevertheless bitter aftertaste. Gold-yellow colour. Hoppy aroma.50 IBU / 18.6 Plato	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11211	Gouden Carolus Ambrio	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	8.0	\N	Gouden Carolus Ambrio is aromatically brewed according to the ancient recipe of the Mechelschen Bruynen. Ambrio is an ’amber’ ale brewed with ’brio’. This white beer of high fermentation finds its origin in the traditional beer of the city of Mechelen. As each city had its own typical beer, the Mechelenians drunk their amber beer: 'Mechelschen Bruynen' for hundreds of years.Our brewery is the only brewery that still brews this type of beer. According to the tradition the basic recipe of this beer dates from 1421 and is therefore the oldest beer from the brewery.The current version is slightly heavier than the original and finer hopped. The balance between the different malts, the fine hops and typical aromas with herbs ensure that this beer combines the whole-hearted nature of brown beers with the freshness of blonde beers.This flavored and spicy light brown tasting beer should be served fairly fresh. Refermentation in the bottle.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11212	Gouden Carolus Cuvée Van De Keizer Imperial Blond (Rood Label)	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	10.0	\N	Gouden Carolus Cuvée van de Keizer Rood is a strong blond beer that was launched in 2008 on the occasion of '10 years Gouden Carolus Cuvée van de Keizer Blauw'. However, it contains more types of malt and 3 different kinds of herbs are added during the brewing process.Its bright golden color, high alcohol percentage and full and well-balanced taste make this ale a genuine source of vitality and power which will please even the most critical connoisseur.For ideal savoring, gently pour out in one fluent movement, at a temperature of 7-8° C (45-46°F). Proudly poured it is savored with respect. Those who like a refreshing, heavy and somewhat spicy beer, choose this blonde ale.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11213	Lucifer	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	8.0	\N	Lucifer entered the market in the early 1980s under the label of the Riva brewery. It was an extension to the popular segment of strong, blond beers. In 2009, brewery Het Anker obtained the right to brew and commercialize Lucifer.Lucifer is a strong, blond beer (8.0%) with a gold yellow color and creamy white head. Its fruity aroma with subtle notes of bitter hops, followed by a long and perfectly balanced finish, will definitely seduce you!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11214	Maneblusser	5289	Belgian Ale	5.8	\N	Brewery Het Anker decided to brew an easy drinkable city beer for the Mechelenians, still peppy enough in order to enjoy it to the fullest. We brew a heroic beer called Maneblusser. It’s a blond beer with an alcohol percentage of 5.8% vol. in which you can taste a subtle citrus aroma and a fine finish. Maneblusser is brewed according to the traditional method of high fermentation with refermentation in the bottle.The inspiration for this brew originates in the night of January 27th in the year 1687. The moon projected its reddish glow on Saint Rumbold’s tower, which was wrapped in a dense fog. “Fire, fire, the tower is on fire!” shouts the dreary voice of a drunken man. The alarm was sounded and people were making haste to help extinguish the so-called fire. Before the tower was reached, the moon slowly moved through the fog. From that moment on, the Mechelenians are called the Maneblussers or “Moonextinguishers”.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11229	Mechelschen Bruynen	5289	Belgian Ale	6.0	\N	Replaced in 2005 by Gouden Carolus Ambrio 6.5%In the past, every town in Belgium had its own beer typical of the area. Hence, some centuries ago, the people of Mechelen drank a beer known as 'Mechelschen Bruynen' or 'Mechelen Brown'. Our Brewery is the only one still brewing this type of beer. The recipe has its origin at the 14th century. The nowadays version is a little more heavy and contains more hops. The balance between the different malts, the fine hops and typical tastes of spices creates a perfect harmony beween the powerful taste of brown beers and the freshness of the blond beers.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11257	Vossen Met De Meynen	5289	Belgian Ale	6.5	\N	\N	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11215	Gouden Carolus Cuvée Van De Keizer Whisky Infused	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	11.7	\N	Brouwerij Het Anker herlanceert ’Whisky Infused’ op algemene vraag. In 2015 verscheen dit speciaalbier als 1ste smaakexpressie van de ’Gouden Carolus Indulgence’ reeks. Dit is een serie gelimiteerde bieren die jaarlijks met wisselende inhoud worden uitgebracht. Dit bier werd meteen uitgeroepen tot ’World’s Best Spirit Flavoured Beer’ op de World Beer Awards (U.K., 2016).Zjef De Loose, marketing medewerker bij de brouwerij bevestigt: “Bijna 2 jaar na de lancering krijgt de brouwerij nog dagelijks vraag naar ’Whisky Infused’. Daarom is er besloten om het bier een vaste plaats in ons biergamma te geven onder de merknaam “Gouden Carolus Cuvée van de Keizer Whisky Infused”. Die naam lag voor de hand, want voor dit brouwsel wordt Gouden Carolus Cuvée van de Keizer Blauw verrijkt met een infusie van Gouden Carolus Single Malt whisky. Dat resulteert in een krachtig en volmondig bier met subtiele toetsen van vanille, eikenhout en chocolade.'Dit weekend zal Gouden Carolus Cuvée van de Keizer Whisky Infused in primeur te proeven zijn op het Zythos Bier Festival. Vanaf volgende week vind je de flessen bij de betere drankenhandel, Delhaize supermarkten en in het bezoekerscentrum aan Brouwerij Het Anker en Stokerij De Molenberg.Gouden Carolus Single Malt is een verfijnde whisky gedistilleerd uit het moutbeslag van het bier Gouden Carolus Tripel. De opeenvolgende rijping in klassieke Bourbon vaten gevolgd door een verdere rijping in Het Anker vaten (houten vaten bewerkt door de tonnenmaker volgens onze eigen specificaties) resulteert in een verfijnde whisky met een volle en evenwichtige smaak. De subtiel aanwezige fruitaroma’s worden mooi aangevuld met toetsen van hout en vanille.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11216	Gouden Carolus Easter (2010+)	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	10.5	\N	Gouden Carolus Easter Ale is brewed once a year to commemorate Easter. It is a golden ale that is rich, full bodied and full of flavor and life. This ale was brewed and intended to drink with Easter dinner. This special brew may be laid down, it will increase in complexity and balance as years pass.Gouden Carolus Easter Ale is the most limited production brew from the Het Anker brewery. Only 2000 cases are brewed each year. The 2010 edition is a Dark Brown Ale at 9% ABV.The 2011+ edition states Golden Ale on the label but is also a Dark Brown Ale at 10% ABV.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11217	Blond	5289	Belgian Ale	6.5	\N	Anker Blonde is brewed artisnally with the best natural ingredients by the established Anker Brewery since 1369. This top fermented lager is very refreshing thanks to its balance between pale malt and refined hops. Tastes quite fresh at 6° - 8° C.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
11218	Gouden Carolus Easter Beer (2007-2009)	5289	Belgian Strong Ale	10.5	\N	Blond rich beer that is brewed each year during the easter period. It contains several types of malt and during brewing 3 herbs are added.This pleasant golden blond beer is chosen for he who loves a richer, somewhat spicy and refreshing beer.Disclaimer: This entry is for the vintages from Gouden Carolus Easter Beer from 2007 to 2009 onwards.  Before it was a dark beer.  In 2007 the recipe changed to a blond beer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:43.748239	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
