12830	Bufcafe	5305	American Pale Ale (APA)	5.4	\N	The science behind roasting and brewing extends beyond the brewery.  And a brewer’s (second) best friend is a great cup of coffee.  This prompted us to conduct a little experiment with our friends at Detour Coffee Roasters.  We combined a single-hop pale ale with freshly brewed BufCafe Rwandan coffee.  The result is a beautiful blend of hop-induced tropical fruitiness, fruity tamarind, orange and stone fruit from the coffee beans.  We didn’t want to mask these flavours and aromas behind malt sweetness or roast.  Instead, we highlighted the amazing combination of some of the world’s best coffee and hops.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.316389	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
12837	Higher Dimension	5305	Belgian Ale	7.5	\N	Higher Dimension, a Belgian Amber dry-hopped with Ella, has aromas of bubble gum and candy sugar, which are contrasted with floral and tropical zest characters. The tropical, spicy hop notes shine up-front, giving way to malt sweetness, balanced against a grapefruit backbone.Under the “Higher Dimension, Higher Cause” effort, Nickel Brook will be donating partial proceeds from the beer to the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR), an agency that “works to ensure that everybody has the right to seek asylum and find safe refuge in another country.”	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.316389	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
