12995	Kaleidoscopic Dreamscape	5307	American Strong Ale	8.0	\N	Kaleidoscopic Dreamscape is an imperial version of a new style that we would like to christen as an India Cream Ale; the next logical evolution of an extremely juicy, soft, creamy, and hop forward IPA that has a low residual bitterness, and is brewed with huge amounts of milk sugar. Potent tangerine, apricot, and peach is predominant and complimented by a soft bitterness, with a citrusy aroma and flavor from the addition of lemons and oranges in the whirlpool. Lingering sweetness and a full-bodied creamy mouthfeel provided by the lactose and flaked grain compliment this quadruple dry-hopped ICA.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.316389	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13044	Droplets	5307	American Pale Ale (APA)	5.5	\N	This nifty lilâ€™ super-dry oat pale ale was brewed with a grist containing about 60% flaked oats, flaked rye, and white wheat for supreme fluff. We hit it twice with a hop blend of El Dorado, Calypso, and Nugget. Lots of white grape, mint, and sappy-pear. Juicy. Dry as a bone.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.316389	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13056	Origin Meditation	5307	Mild Ale	4.5	\N	Origin Meditation is our dissertation on British Pub Ales of the past... the hay day of the Burton Union System, a time when oak barrels were â€œthe kegâ€�, and when most British ales contained wild yeast and foreign microbes, some of which would later be classified as Brettanomyces (Yes, the name actually comes from the word Britain). Origin Meditation starts out as a Dark Mild, that is aged in a Bluebird rye whiskey cask, and naturally conditioned for a month on organic maple syrup and a house blend of wild yeast and microbes from our Blendery. Barnyard funk, silky tannins, woody maple and vanilla tones, and a thirst quenching light acidity abound.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13058	The Purp	5307	Sour / Wild Ale	6.0	\N	The Purp is a delicate expression of true, bone dry, lightly acidic, saison brewed with pils and wheat malts, and fermented on our house micro flora and blackberries for 2 months before being naturally conditioned in this oak cask. Served at cellar temperature, and semi sparkling. Funky and bright, lots of mature Blackberry, finishing bone dry, with a light acidity and mild oak tannins.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
