13074	Premium	5307	Sour / Wild Ale	5.0	\N	A wild lagerbier ripened in neutral French oak casks for seven months. Bottle conditioned in vintage green bottles and forcibly light-struck. The gang and I really had a lot fun pulling this one off, without quite knowing what to expect. We wondered what our helles-lager base would do if we threw it into some oak that was inoculated with some #Blendery microbes. The result is mind-bending. Sour and funky, with a gueuze-like complexity. Lemon-zest, honeysuckle, cantaloupe, with a deep mineral profile. Probably the most soft & quaffable beer with this much acidity that I can remember having.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
