13471	Chardonnay Barrel Blonde	5311	Sour / Wild Ale	8.2	\N	The second release from the Funkwerks brettanomyces inoculated barrels! Smoky, earthy aromas from the brettanomyces play off the oakiness of our Chardonnay barrels, combined with a slightly sweet fruitiness of a high gravity Saison; this makes for a complex beer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13475	Motif	5311	Belgian Strong Ale	8.8	\N	This high gravity Saison starts with a blend of Belgian and German malts combined with cane sugar and brown sugar from Malawi and rounded out with German, Belgian, and Czech hops. Flavor notes of candied apricots, black pepper, rum and ginger are purely from a unique Saison yeast strain and a warm primary fermentation. The finish is dry and crisp with a noticeable alcohol warming. Brewed by Jeff Blackburn at Funkwerks.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13476	Danny'S Gold Mine	5311	Belgian Strong Ale	10.0	\N	This is a nice beer.  Brewed in honor of Danny Williams Danny’s Gold Mine is a collaboration between Funkwerks, Crooked Stave, New Belgium, Odell Brewing Co. and Ska Brewing.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13477	Brett Trois	5311	Sour / Wild Ale	7.7	\N	Say 'hello' to Funkwerks’ first Brettanomyces-only fermentation! This light and refreshing brew demonstrates the funky flavors produced by the Belgian Brettanomyces strain used. A fruity bubblegum aroma is followed by a crisp citrus flavor. We used a large amount of Galaxy, Rakau, and Crystal hops toward the end of the boil and for the dry hop addition to contribute tropical fruit flavors and aromas such as passion fruit, papaya, and mango while also imparting gentle citrus notes. The mouth tingling effervescence with tart pineapple finish and biscuit backbone exemplifies characteristics common to this Brettanomyces strain.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13478	Barrel-Aged Dahlia	5311	Belgian Ale	7.5	\N	Our first foeder beer. Rich and complex malt aroma, hints of sweet caramel and fruit esters. Characteristics of chocolate, raisins, and a hint of red wine.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
