13481	Cochon	5311	Belgian Ale	6.3	\N	Our house saison yeast meets an American pale ale. Generous late additions of Cascade and Centennial hops give a floral and citrus aroma that blends with the fruity and peppery notes from our Saison yeast. The flavor brings a hint of citrus which yields to hop bitterness and peppery phenols in the dry finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
13494	Barrel-Aged Brett Trois	5311	Sour / Wild Ale	7.7	\N	This barrel-aged experiment was originally one of Funkwerks’ first and only primary  Brettanomyces-only fermentation. A large mount of Galaxy, Rakau, and Crystal hops were added toward the end of the boil and for the dry hop addition, contributing to the tropical fruit flavors and aromas. We wanted to experiment with the wild yeast and Brett yeast by putting it in red wine barrels. Bright tropical fruit aroma, white grape like character, slight tart pineapple and a hint of vanilla.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.519471	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
