14497	Birra Di Natale	587	Belgian Strong Ale	8.0	\N	Birra speciale, prodotta con lieviti ad alta fermentazione, di colore ambrato carico con riflessi fulvi, dalla schiuma cremosa, fine e persistente. All’olfatto ci regala una suadente fragranza di caramello, vaniglia, frutta matura e cacao di Guanaja. La lieve frizzantezza esalta il corpo rotondo ed importante con delicati sentori di malto. Abbinamento: cappone ripieno, formaggi erborinati, frutta secca, panettone. Temperatura di servizio 8 - 10° C. Special beer, brewed with top-fermenting yeast, a strong amber color with tawny hues, creamy, fine and persistent foam. The nose gives us a mellow fragrance of caramel, vanilla, ripe fruit and cocoa Guanaja. The slight carbonation enhances the round and important body with delicate hints of malt. Pairing: capon stuffed, blue cheese, dried fruit, cake. Serving temperature 8 - 10° C.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.888783	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
14498	Senza Glutine	587	Golden Ale / Blond Ale	5.0	\N	Birra a bassa fermentazione ottenuta selezionando i migliori malti, non filtrata e non pastorizzata. All'olfatto offre freschi sentori di cereale, fieno e fiori bianchi. Il corpo è maltato in armonia con il delicato amaro del luppolo. Piacere puro senza glutine. Abbinamenti: carni bianche, pesci delicati, trota salmonata e formaggi freschi. Servire a 5 - 6° C. Ingredienti: acqua, malto d'orzo, luppolo, lievito.Low fermentation beer obtained by selecting the best malts, unfiltered and unpasteurized. On the nose it offers fresh hints of corn, hay and white flowers. The body is malted in harmony with the delicate bitterness of the hops. Pure pleasure gluten free. Pairings: poultry, delicate fish, rainbow trout and fresh cheeses. Serve at 5 - 6° C. Ingredients: water, barley malt, hops, yeast.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.888783	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
14526	Native Series - Tennessee Cream Ale	5321	Cream Ale	6.3	\N	Tennessee Cream Ale, the second release in our Native Family of beers, draws its inspiration from the rich agricultural and culinary heritage that guides our brewing program. Corn has long been a staple crop of the South, whether being served at the table or sipped from a jar, and was traditionally used as the base ingredient for the Cream Ale style of beer. In celebration of that heritage, we have crafted a light golden Tennessee Cream Ale brewed with flaked corn and heirloom grits, and fermented with a wild strain of native yeast from our Farm for a delicately malty body with a hint of corn sweetness and a crisp, refreshing finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:44.888783	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
