19036	Barrel Aged Brown Ale No. 2 (Chardonnay Oak Barrel)	715	Brown Ale	7.0	\N	Here at YellowBelly we didn’t think there was anything we could do to make our beer taste better. We were wrong. We have begged, borrowed and stolen some oak barrels from vineyards, craft distilleries and the odd one from the local mayor’s private wine cellar and aged our beer in them.This bottle, when treated with care, can be cellared for many years and will improve with age.For more info on this particular bottle and the barrel it was aged in, please visit our website.www.simonlambertandsons.ieIngredientsMalts: Chateau Pilsen, Cara Blond, Special B, Wheat. Hops: Hallertauer Hersbrucker, Fuggles. Yeast: WLP023 Burton Ale.StorageFrench Chardonnay Oak Barrel	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.444456	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19073	The Baron	715	Amber Ale	4.5	\N	Our American style red ‘IPA’ was brewed with our Head Brewers favourite malt combo-Red X and Cara Hell.For the hops, we choose only one; fresh as ya like ColombusHops in the mash. Hops in the empty kettle. Hops in the full kettle. Hops at flame out. Hops in the whirlpool. Hops with the yeast. Hops after fermentation. Hops before cold crashing. There were alot of hop additions in this beer and every single Columbus addition has added a layer of that stereotypical west coast flavour. Enjoy fresh. Enjoy often.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.608724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
