19226	Under My Tree-Roof Slanting Lines Of April Rain Separate To Drops	5373	Sour / Wild Ale	6.2	\N	Wild Ale with Sudachi and White TeaGravity: 13.9 PMalts: Pils, Wheat, Oat MaltHops: Sterling, AhtanumSecret Ingredients: Sudachi, White Tea, Poems of Matsuo Bashõ(from label)Tasting NotesSudachi adds a complex citrus character intermingled with the mild tartness and floral notes from our wild house culture. Mid-pallet is reminiscent of lemon tart, preserved limes and meringue fading into the softness of white tea.Beer nerd factsSudachi is a seldom seen Asian citrus fruit akin to yuzu but with a deeper, more complex character. Poetry by Matsuo Bashõ.Sample Menu DescriptionWild Ale with Sudachi and White Tea. Mild tartness and floral esters propel the interplay between the deep, preserved lime character of Sudachi (a seldom seen Asian citrus fruit), delicate white tea and the haikus of Basho.(from http://www.offcolorbrewing.com/sellrain)Expect tartness and floral esters to propel the interplay between the deep, preserved lime character of Sudachi (a seldom seen Asian citrus fruit), delicate white tea, and the haikus of Basho. While this beer is named after one of those haikus, we’ll let you call it “April Rain” to make ordering easier.(from http://www.facebook.com/OffColorBrewing/videos/1978475142259750)	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.608724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
