19230	/ Perennial / Side Project Procatstination (2018)	5373	Sour / Wild Ale	5.1	\N	Wine Barrel aged Wild AleGravity: 12.5 PMalts: Pils, Vienna, SpeltHops: Nugget, KazbekSecret Ingredients: 2016 Procatstination Barrel LeesBrewed to benefit: The Wildlife Sanctuary(from label)It all started with a fundraiser for the Wildcat Sanctuary, organized by the fine folks at Chicago's Northdown Cafe. And we teamed up with some of our fave Mid(wild)west buds Perennial and Side Project to create a special brew for the occasion. And while the event is no longer (we miss you, Northdown!), it lives on in infamy -- and with this almost-annual-but-not-really release.This year we only have 35 cases! 35! And when all is said and done, we'll be making a donation to the Wildcat Sanctuary. Not only to help out the big cats, but in memory of our great friends at Northdown and the amazing party that was Lions, Tigers, and Beers.White grapes, nectarine and preserved lemon with an intense citric acidity like the icy feeling of looking out into the darkness and seeing hungry, peering eyes staring back at you. Fortunately, that's just the cat though and it's hard to explain that breakfast is late because of daylights saving time to cats.(from http://www.offcolorbrewing.com/releases)	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.608724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
19231	Reine Des Renards	5373	Sour / Wild Ale	8.3	\N	Flemish Blonde style ale fermented in a Calvados foedre with raw apple ciderand native yeastsGravity: 15.5 PMalts: Pils, Vienna, CarawheatHops: NuggetSecret Ingredients: Raw apple cider pressed by Ryan Burk, Native flora, 14 year old French Calvados Foedre(from label)Flemish Blonde (similar in nature to the more widely known Flemish Reds) fermented for five months in a 14 year old French Calvados foedre with our wild yeasts. Then refermented for six more months with 900 liters of raw apple cider (Northern Pippen, Northern Spy, and Golden Delicious), unpasteurized to preserve their native flora. And pressed by our good friend, Ryan Burk, who you’ll probably recognized as that devastatingly handsome lumberjack, hipster looking guy from all those Angry Orchard commercials.(from http://www.offcolorbrewing.com/releases)	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.608724	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
