20246	American Hop Surgeon	5386	American Strong Ale	8.6	\N	Cattle Baron’s Ball Winner #2: American Hop Surgeon Imperial American Nut-Brown AleThis Imperial American Nut Brown Ale is the result of our 2nd groundbreaking collaboration from the 2015 Cattle Baron’s Ball in Akron to benefit the American Cancer Society. It features full-bodied malt flavor with an abundance of caramelized taste, complemented by hints of roastiness from the finest Belgian chocolate malt. But it doesn’t stop there - its complex and satisfying profile is enhanced with a good amount of American hop character for a great flavor and aroma. It has a little of everything to make all beer lovers smile, including the typical antioxidant properties imparted from hops. Live long and prosper, Captain!!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
20258	Gavel Slammer	5386	American Strong Ale	17.4	\N	An over-the-top ale like no other, with a gavel-slammin’ flavor profile - rich, aromatic, lively and dark.  Going light years over the top of Ohio’s old beer/alcohol limit, Gavel Slammer is brewed to celebrate Hoppin’ Frog putting the hammer down for freedom in brewing Ohio’s beer!  Because of our efforts, on August 26th 2016 we were presented the actual gavel used in the final Senate session that removed Ohio’s alcohol limit on beer!! We did our little part, and we’re proud of this recognition, and our freedom.Specifications: 17.4% Alc./Vol 1.158 OG (35.9 Plato) 65 IBU	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
20297	Hipster Ale	5388	American Pale Ale (APA)	5.5	\N	Perhaps you heard of a worldwide beer-movement that tributes favorite hipster neighbourhoods across the globe. First came Istedgade, Copenhagen then Södermalm, Stockholm followed by Williamsburg, New York and Shoreditch, London accompanied by Trastevere, Rome & last El Raval, Barcelona. If you feel excluded because you’re hip but your city is not, this cutting-edge, ‘hip without borders’ pale ale is an homage to you – the global hipster. Cheers!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
