20486	Mango Suprise Ipa	5394	American Pale Ale (APA)	7.0	\N	Sail away to the tropics with our new mango infused IPA! Golden in color, like that of a sunset in the islands, it’s body is gently topped with a frothy white sea foam head. Tropical aromas of mango, pineapple, papaya and citrus gently play off a bright hop profile with a slight malt nose. Flavors follow the aroma but expose the juicy hop bitterness and flavor of Simcoe, Amarillo, and Summit hops with a slight hint of Pilsner and CaraPils malt. The relatively dry malt body is gently accentuated by the sweet mango flavors, brought straight from the islands of Barbados.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
20489	Barrel Aged Loch-Up Scotch Ale	5394	Scotch Ale / Wee Heavy	12.0	\N	Scotch Ale aged in oak bourbon barrels.Per the brewer, this is a different beer than Bourbon Barrel Loch Down, as it is 2% stronger and aged in bourbon barrels longer (some first-use and some second-use bourbon barrels blended together).	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
20490	Brigid'S Irish Red	5394	Irish Red Ale	5.0	\N	The story of Brigid (pronounced 'Breed') is one shrouded in mystery; equal parts pagan history and Catholic sainthood, the one thing that seems to hold true is that she embodies the fiery spirit of Ireland. Our paean to her is held within the confines of a fine Irish-style red ale, a proud exultation that is bright, bold, and smooth. Brewed with molasses for a hint of jammy dark fruit, low-medium hints of earthy hops come through, and creamy malt provides a calming backbone. A modest alcohol content keeps everything convivial, as there’s plenty to toast come early spring.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:46.949817	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
