20740	Pacific Pale Ale	5399	American Pale Ale (APA)	4.0	\N	Tropical fruit flavours and aroma on a light malt base.The Australian and New Zealand craft brewing scene has taken inspiration from the hoppy aromatic Pacific Coast American craft beers to come up with a beer style of its own.Meantime’s interpretation shouts passion fruit, mango and grapefruit, succulent and soft pale malt. A tropical taste for wholehearted summer drinking. Goes well with strong pepper flavours such as jerk chicken, also rich soft cheeses.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.120099	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
20747	(College Beer Club) Long-Aged Abbey Ale	5399	Belgian Strong Ale	6.9	\N	Brewed on 26th February 2009. Abbey then spent several months in Syrah casks before maturing in the bottle for a further 18 months. A pale ale malt brew with 5% crystal in the grist and 17 degrees plato original gravity gave a beer that was 6.8% ABV on bottling and which now weighs in at 6.9%. Goldings hops early and late, plus a Special Belgian Abbey Ale yeast complete the picture.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.120099	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
20767	(College Beer Club) Scotch Ale Oak Aged	5399	Scotch Ale / Wee Heavy	7.5	\N	The Scotch style is generally associated with Edinburgh where ist is said to have originated in the 18th century.Boiled for longer than most Scottish beers it has a wonderful red-meets-brown colour in the glass. The distance from Southern Englands hop gardens meant that like most Scottish beers this is a relatively lightly hopped beer. Scotch ales were definitley not an everyday drink, and were certainly intended to be special occasion beers.We therefore recommend that you reserve this beer for a special occasion, like, say, when you are feeling exceptionally pleased with yourself	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.120099	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
