25051	Wild Patriot	5449	Sour / Wild Ale	6.4	\N	An American Wild Ale aged in French oak barrels previously used for white wine.  We also added red, white, and the very rare blue oak chips to the barrel for further aging.This wild ale was fermented in an American oak barrel previously used for white wine. Seasoned oak chips were added from red, white and blue oak trees and let the natural yeasts on the wood go to work. What came out was a very patriotic brett-forward ale with lots of complex aromas and flavors. Blue oak? Never heard of it. In fact no one we could find had either, yet we were being told it existed. A quick Internet search and sure enough, blue oak. Much rarer than the red and white oak common to California, 'Mr. Blue Oak' is very picky on where he wants to grow and not easily obtainable, he hides. But what Mr. Blue Oak didn’t know is that a certain brother of a certain brewer happens to live right where Mr. Blue Oak likes to hide, and had no problem grabbing a few of his sneaky wood branches to add to our brew. Thanks to Shayne, Libertine 1, Mr. Blue Oak 0.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
