25211	Tcen Tcen Cream Ale Special Brew	877	Cream Ale	5.9	\N	Oatmeal pre-prohibbition Cream Ale.Brewed for the 10th anniversary of the pub Pazzeria in Milan.If you are Italian and ~40 years old, you will probably look for the 'Manerba Ifix' too.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25080	Bébé Feet	5449	Sour / Wild Ale	6.4	\N	This wild ale was fermented with old growth zin grapes found on an abandoned winery site from the early California Mission days. Hand picked and then foot stomped by the brewer’s 2 year old daughter, Aubree.The juice was left on the grape skins for 10 days before being filtered and drained into the already fermenting wild ale wort in French red wine (Pinot Noir) barrels.Uncovering these Mission-era vines was like discovering a mysterious treasure.What style were these grapes? Would they mature for use? How would they taste? Who abandoned this winery?The big question.... Would we fall to our deaths from the 20ft ladder precariously propped up the side of a gnarled old oak tree while trying to pick the last few clusters from a vine struggling for sunlight at the top of the tree?Most were never answered, but what we did find was an exceptional wild ale, tart and dry, with a touch of the wild grapes left on the finish. This brew can never be recreated exactly like this again so make sure to try this before its gone forever.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25083	Brett Proof Raspberry	5449	Sour / Wild Ale	6.6	\N	Brett Proof wild ale is a blend of two very different brews. One a highly tart, dry and acidic beer aged in locally-grown organic fruits from 4 Elements Farm. The other was a subtle berlinerweisse-style ale, with a much fuller mouth feel and hints of brettanomyces aged in a bourbon barrel.750ml bottles released on 6/28/2014 with raspberries.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25084	Sour Pomegranate Porter	5449	Sour / Wild Ale	6.2	\N	\N	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25087	Heard It Through The Grapevine	5449	Sour / Wild Ale	6.5	\N	Heard it Through the Grapevine is a golden wild ale aged on raisins that were sourced specifically for this brew from our friend Phil Ogden’s family farm in the Central Valley. This boozy and oaky wild ale has hints of tobacco and plumbs and is reminiscent of an almond champagne.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25090	Heard It Through The Grapevine 2017	5449	Sour / Wild Ale	8.4	\N	A sophisticated red ale that was brewed specifically to age on the raisins we used in this brew. After removing the fruit we blended the beer with our Golden ale until we found a nice balance between the sour and the sweetness from the additional sugars. Intense aromas and flavors ofport, raisins,Cabernet grapes, plums and black cherries with a sour finish. Find yourself a nice cigar or a rich Chocolate cake for this dessert-y summer sipper.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25100	California Amber	5450	Amber Ale	5.5	\N	A rich, copper ale with a case full of gold medals. Our California Amber takes its inspiration from traditional English ESBs. Four types of malts give it a bold complexity, and our proprietary yeast strain lends it a fruity, madeira-like richness. However, it’s the American hops that give this ale a distinct bite and floral aroma that have earned it just about every major beer medal.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25109	Tongue Buckler Imperial Red Ale	5450	American Strong Ale	10.0	\N	100 IBUsBottled Version:  107 IBUs, 10%Prepare to walk the plank to an Ale of overwhelming proportions. More hops & more malts than any land lubber can handle. After this experience...your tongue will be buckled. The I.B.U.’s (International Bitterness Units) are off the scale on this ale. Be forewarned, those with a timid palate, this is not a wee beer! Handcrafted in small batches for those sailing the seas in search of great ales.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25114	Calm Before The Storm	5450	Cream Ale	5.5	\N	A coffee ale with a touch of cream.Calm Before the Storm came from a quest for a warm weather alternative to our Victory at Sea Imperial Porter. Like its more robust cousin, we infuse a punch of flavor using cold brewed Caffé Calabria coffee and a hint of vanilla. But this time, we added it to a lighter-bodied golden cream ale. The end result is a surprisingly bright, coffee-forward beer that’s perfectly refreshing. Previously listed at 6.2% abv.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
