25151	Piper Down Scottish Ale - Barrel Aged	5450	Scotch Ale / Wee Heavy	5.8	\N	Our Piper Down Scottish Ale hits all the right notes for the Ballast Point Bagpipe Corps that inspired it. We created this very low hopped, malty ale for the band to enjoy using UK Maris Otter malt, roasted barley, UK hops and low fermentation temperatures. Then we let the brew’s sweet complexity build over a three-hour boil. Full of roasted caramel flavor, it’s a pub classic with Ballast Point personality.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
25163	Tongue Buckler Imperial Red Ale - Bourbon Barrel Aged	5450	American Strong Ale	10.0	\N	Is it right?  Seems a bit excessive really.  But we did it anyway, because we can.  We have aged our Tongue Buckler Imperial Red Ale in bourbon barrels and it is ready to drink.  Yep, that 10% ABV monstrosity has been, as they say, kicked up a notch.It was a quick stay in the barrel.  We didn’t want the beer to lose all of it’s hallmark hoppiness.  And after only a couple of months, a lot remains.  Flavors of vanilla and oak now intertwine with the malty sweetness and are countered by a pronounced hop bitterness.  What was complex is now impossible to unravel.  It really has to be tasted to be understood.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
