26082	/ New Belgium Darksynth	5462	Sour / Wild Ale	0.0	\N	A blend of 50% New Belgium Oscar, 40% Upland Dantalion, and 10% Upland Raspberry Lambic. Oscar is a darker base sour, with notes of chocolate, green apple, and cherry, which is a main contributor to La Folie creation. Dantalion is Upland’s take on an Oud Bruin, with spices added for complexity, including star anise, ginger, and grains of paradise. Raspberry Lambic is the addition of over 3 lbs. of fresh whole raspberries to a base lambic-style beer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
26083	Viola	5462	Sour / Wild Ale	0.0	\N	Viola was developed by creating a small beer from a larger batch of Dantalion. The wort underwent a long kettle boil, over 12 hours, with hops grown at our brewery added throughout. Only 5 white oak barrels received the beer the next day, and a 3 month fermentation process yielded a beer with polite lactic acid character, caramelized kettle character, and light hop aroma. Viola was aged on edible violas for one month prior to packaging to add floral flavors and aromas.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
