26126	Cauldron	5462	Sour / Wild Ale	0.0	\N	The nature of brewing inherently involves the combination of ingredients to create that final well balanced beer.  Inside this vessel resides one part Malefactor, Epic Flanders-style red ale, and one part Dantalion Dark Wild Ale.  These beers were blended and aged on Northern Michigan Montmorency cherries.  The melding of these tow beers creates a complex sour ale with notes of spices, charred oak and copious cherry fruit character.  Blended to be enjoyed by the Alchemist in all of us.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
26128	/ Country Boy Funk Land Country Shuffle	5462	Sour / Wild Ale	0.0	\N	Funk Land Country Shuffle brings the funk in this collaboration with our good friends at Country Boy Brewing in Lexington, KY. This beer is a blend of two spontaneously fermented beers, Creek and Quarry, along with Basis. We aged the beer in barrels from Country Boy and added Balaton cherries, cocoa nibs and chocolate mint. You can expect aromas of dark cherries and mint with flavors of fruity funk and hints of chocolate.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
26131	Project Babylon Pale Ale	5463	American Pale Ale (APA)	4.6	\N	Cask, keykeg, can & bottle; RegularOriginally released in 2015 as Project Babylon as part of the Small Batch series.Note: The labels & pump clips currently have 'Pale Ale' in large text with 'Project Babylon' in much smaller print above, so it is easy to miss. There is not a separate beer called Gun Pale Ale.A classic American Pale Ale brewed using a combination of very pale malts and American hops. Vibrant, refreshing and zesty on the nose, with citrus notes and a dry finish on the palate. A beer for hop lovers.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.985308	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
