27689	Spring Brew	5478	Golden Ale / Blond Ale	4.3	\N	Cask; Seasonal - March & April.A fresh, hoppy, delightful golden ale to welcome in the bright new season. You will love this zesty brew, full of tasty tropical flavours to enliven the taste buds.Style: Golden hopped ale.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
27690	Ruck & Roll	5478	Bitter Ale	4.0	\N	Brewed to coincide with the climax of the rugby season. Ruck and Roll is a classic 4% abv English style Pale Ale. Amber in colour with a full, yet very dry palate balanced by succulent fruity hops. This is a classic cask conditioned beer with depth, structure and integrity.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
27691	/ Brecon / Bru / Inveralmond / Purity Celtic Cross	5478	Irish Red Ale	4.5	\N	Cask: Special - 2014On more exciting news, we’ve been invited to brew in the famous St. Austell’s Brewery in Cornwall a ‘Celtic Collaboration’ Brew with fellow breweries Brecon (Wales), Inveralmond (Scotland) and Purity (England). Here, we’ll bring a bit of Ireland to 160BBL (26k litres) brew to be distributed all over the UK and Ireland – get your orders in!! The brew will take place on the 1st of November and beer ready beginning of December. Never been done before so a definite collectors item.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
27692	Jolly Holly	5478	Bitter Ale	4.3	\N	A rich, dark winter ale with a difference with the addition of American Simcoe hops to deliver a rich and satisfying Christmas brew. See out the year with this appropriately seasonal beer with zesty undertones that harmonise with toasted malts and bring out the Christmas cheer.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
27694	Tamar Creek	5478	Sour / Wild Ale	7.3	\N	If you are familiar with the sour red ales of East Flanders, you are going to love Tamar Creek. If not, prepare to be surprised, and we hope amazed and delighted by the sheer complexity of flavour that can be found in beer. This strong ale is brewed in our brewery and matured in oak casks for over twelve months, during which time it takes on a vinous character and tart sourness. For the last few months we add whole cherries, hand-picked from Burcombe cherry trees at Bohetheric Farm in the heart of the Tamar valley. Served in a wine glass or a chalice, this unfiltered beer pours ruby red, perhaps with a little natural haze and a hint of primrose blush in the foam. The aroma is of distinctive ripe cherries, blended with oak and a sharp acidity. The palate is initially dry but as it lingers in the mouth, the complex sweetness of malt, oak and fruit come through, providing the depth and complexity of a vintage port. Tamar Creek is a live beer and its flavour will continue to develop if stored in a cool dry place for several years. Bottle, 750ml.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
27695	Eureka	5478	American Pale Ale (APA)	4.9	\N	Back by popular demand, Eureka APA was the first of our globally inspired beers, brewed by Roger Ryman in collaboration with Rob Lovatt, Head Brewer at Thornbridge Brewery, using the exciting new Eureka hop variety and crafted in the style of American Pale Ales from West Coast USA that inspired a brewing generation.  Eureka is a single hopped APA using Maris Otter barley blended with crystal rye malt to create a flash of amber, alongside a little flaked maize for crispness.  Thornbridge ale yeast in the fermentation provides a light and delicate canvas that allows the new ‘Eureka’ hop to express all of its distinctive character.  Intense notes of blackcurrant, tangerine and grapefruit come through alongside strong herbal and hop-kiln aromas for a taste sensation that promises we are going to be hearing a lot more about this hop in the future.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
27696	Skipper	5478	American Pale Ale (APA)	4.9	\N	Mitchells & Butlers’ Castle pubs are about to get a new addition, courtesy of a partnership between Boston-based Harpoon and Cornish St Austell Brewery.Skipper (4.9% abv), a limited edition American Pale Ale, has been brewed in collaboration with the breweries after the Harpoon team embarked on a fact finding mission in Blighty last summer and happened upon St Austell.Roger Ryman, St Austell Brewery’s head brewer, repaid the visit with a trip to Boston in March this year and got involved in producing a collaborative ale between the two breweries.As well as brewing it at Harpoon Brewery, which is one of the top 10 craft breweries in the USA (don’t you know), Ryman returned from the States and brewed the same recipe in St Austell’s small batch brewery.‘Skipper utilises all-English ingredients combined with USA flair and delivers a classic pale ale with a contemporary twist. We’re really pleased with the end result, and that it has launched in Castle pubs,’ Ryman said.The skippy amber cask ale boasts blackcurrant and lychee aromas and the team says it has a bitter and rich fruit finish.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
