27698	The Gribbin (Cask)	5478	Bitter Ale	4.3	\N	Cask; Special.St Austell Brewery and National Trust have teamed together to create a limited edition seasonal pale ale called The Gribbin, to celebrate 50 years of looking after the coast and named after the headland that the brewery helped secure for the National Trust to look after forever in 1965.Using all British ingredients, our head Brewer Roger Ryman has created this limited edition English Pale Ale to celebrate the 50th anniversary of St Austell Brewery’s gift to the National Trust.Pale Amber in colour, Gribbin Ale offers a fragant aroma full of blackcurrants. On the palate is firm and dry balanced by bursting summer fruits.At 4.3% abv this is a beer with depth and character that will not dissapoint!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.492062	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
