28051	Dymaxion	5482	American Pale Ale (APA)	6.2	\N	We packed this outrageously crushable beverage with Nelson, Rakau, Motueka, & Mosaic hops, yielding an intensely aromatic profile that marries a bouquet of tropical characteristics with crisp, biting citrus over a dry malt backbone. Prepare your taste-buddies for a stunningly refreshing testament to some of New Zealand’s most fearlessly innovative hop producers.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
28090	Funky Fruitlands - Apricot	5482	Sour / Wild Ale	6.2	\N	Fruitlands has now firmly established itself within our lineup as both a bastion of unparalleled crushability and as a beer that lends itself extremely graciously to experimentation, hence this little gem. We upgraded this latest iteration of our beloved fruited gose to a penthouse suite in Flavor Tower by fermenting the kettle-soured wort with our house Brett strains and dialing the apricot addition up to 11. The resulting beer is a rollicking cascade of funky, fruity refreshment that rolls down the taste buds like your own personal second-line parade.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
28093	Palace Of Paper Sacks	5482	Sour / Wild Ale	7.8	\N	For Palace of Paper Sacks, we set aside a few barrels of our white wine barrel-aged sour blond and stuffed each one with 50 pounds of local, heirloom nectarines. After months of mingling in the barrel, the resulting beer is a powerful & complex fruited sour beer with loads of nectarine aroma and flavor. Fermentation begins with our house Lomaland yeast culture and is then followed with a secondary fermentation by an alarmingly diverse array of sour & funky cultures. It’s a massive pain in the ass to make - especially cutting up all those nectarines - so we really hope you dig it.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
28129	Muscle & Mayhem	5483	Sour / Wild Ale	5.0	\N	Gigantic! 50 feet of fur & furyTart ale brewed with bananas, coconut, and pineapple.Featuring the BEASTNothing creates a better pairing than beer and board games. It's why we partnered with the creators of Campy Creatures to bring you a collectable series of terrifyingly tasty tart ales featuring creatures from the game.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
28133	Stealth Mode	5483	Sour / Wild Ale	6.0	\N	Tart ale with blueberries. Kettle-soured for a terrifying acidity, this sinister combination of our classic Berliner Weisse style and tart seasonal fruit makes for a scene-stealing explosion of flavor. This beer was brewed in imaginative collaboration with Keymaster Games and is the third of several Campy Creatures we’re bringing to life in themed can releases!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
28147	Red Rover	5483	American Strong Ale	11.3	\N	We’ve partnered with Barks of Love, an all-breed dog rescue organization in Orange County, for a beer inspired by a long weekend hiking the redwoods with man’s best friend. A light toast on the Michter barrels brings a bold bourbon element to this red ale, tempered by the earthy spice of cassia bark and a finishing romp through French Oak. Go fetch!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551538827-9c037cb4f32d?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
