22697	Besviken & Førbannad	5429	Grodziskie/Gose/Lichtenhainer	7.1	\N	«Sur, Besviken och Förbannad – Imperial India Gose» is a fine brew made in collaboration with our good friends from Tempel Brygghus in Uppsala, Sweden. It is a beer brimful of tropical flavors and aromas. Apricot, peach, litchi and pineapple in perfect harmony, with a good dose of coriander and salt. This gives the beer a good complexity with great depth, a sweet mouthfeel and a crisp finish. A base of pale, munich and wheat malts is applied to balance the acidity and the sweeter elements, and a solid dry hopping makes for a fresh finish.Brewed as a collaboration between Tempel Brygghus & 7 Fjell Bryggeri	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22700	Le Glacé	821	Sidro	10.0	\N	Golden blond color, fresh and exuberant mouth-watering scents of hazelnut and peach fragrances. Intense and velvety taste with a dominance of apple followed by a hint of enticing butterscotch and vanilla. Full bodied, finely inlaid balance of acidity and sugar and a very nice length. The must obtained from frozen fruit pressed in January is frozen again. That intensifies sugar concentration before low temperature fermentation begins, which process preserves and seals every flavor and aroma. Excellent from beginning to end, lovely with a foie gras mousse, excellent to enhance blue cheese and delicious with French pastries. McIntosh, Spartan, Empire	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22701	Cid Houblon Api-Hop  Star	821	Sidro	7.0	\N	Extra-sec. Une étonnante fusion de houblon et de pomme, le Cid Api-Hop est fermentée en bouteille et à déguster sur lie. Pomelo et citron excitent l’odorat puis le comblent avec des notes épicées de conifère. En bouche, un bouquet d’agrumes, une pointe d’acidité et une belle rondeur en finale.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22702	Cid Rosé	821	Sidro	6.5	\N	Sec. Nommé meilleur cidre en Amérique du nord en 2016, notre Cid rosé est un produit glamour qui n’aurait jamais vu le jour si Jeannette la corneille avait continué de s’en régaler. La pommette Dolgo était uniquement appréciée des corneilles avant de la transformer. En macérant la pelure de celle-ci, un produit distinct et grâce à cet opportuniste a vu le jour et nous en sommes très fiers!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
