22705	Les Vergers De La Colline Cuvée Précieuse	821	Sidro	8.0	\N	A sumptuous golden color, comforting aromas of wild strawberry jam and crystallized pear tease your gourmet nose followed with a floral note of lily of the valley. Its complexity unfolds finely into notes of maple syrup, dried figs, crystallized apricots, buckwheat honey and fresh strawberries. Consistent with traditional cider making, this Cuvée is expertly made from 100% Golden Russet harvested at the peak of Quebec’s winter. Its limited edition production makes it even more precious. For true gourmet, enjoy slowly with canapés, foie gras or fine dark chocolate... and in good company of course!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
22706	Les Vergers De La Colline L'Exotique	821	Sidro	7.5	\N	A rich amber color, a fruity bouquet of banana and litchi with just a tad of clover honey. Silky-smooth banana flavors, the softness of marshmallow and finishing with a tropical note of pineapple. It actually strikes as a very tasty “no man’s land”... original, audacious, class without classification! Innovative, specifically crafted from yellow varieties, it delightfully blends the freshness of ice wine and the unctuous quality of ice cider. Hors d’oeuvres or tapas are needless since this truly is a world in itself ! Excellent apéro or digestif. Whether you offer it, keep it or share it, it’s a definite winner! Gala, Honeycrisp, Jaune Délicieuse	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:47.794426	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
