23750	Brewers Reserve Barley Wine Aged In Bourbon Barrels (13%)	5439	Barley Wine	13.0	\N	Aged in Makers Mark barrels.This is our once a year brew of bourbon barrel aged barley wine. It’s aged in Jack Daniels barrels for a year to allow the beer to mellow out and mature. The oak provides a dimension of coconut, vanilla and even a touch of bourbon. Dark red, low carbonation and great depth, this is one of our most special beers.Malts: Pale malt, Munich, Caramel and roasted malts. Hops: Perle and Saaz. Highly complex aroma of vanilla, caramel, molasses, bourbon, malts.Food pairings: dark chocolate, blue/sharp cheeses.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.124448	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
23712	Whalezbrah!	5438	Bock - Weizenbock	7.5	\N	Surly’s task in welcoming homebrewers to our Upper Midwest turf, then, was to make a true whale for the people who would appreciate it the most. Hence, Whalezbrah!, a beer made exclusively for the 2017 Homebrew Con attendees . In February 2017, we made an impossible-to-replicate oaked pale wheat wort for the American Homebrewers Association wort rally hosted at our MSP facility. Do not ask us how we did this. Feel free to speculate, get out a white board and make a T-chart for all we care, but it’s a secret. We took the same wort 500+ homebrewers brought home from the rally, so we brewed it, aged it in virgin oak with Brettanomyces, and the result is Whalezbrah! It’s tart, a little funky from the barrel-aging, wheat-y, and has a unique oak character that will please beer nerds and noobs alike.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.124448	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
