24289	Modern Helles	5443	Helles	4.1	\N	Modern Helles is a traditional Bavarian session beer that’s refreshingly uncomplicated in style. We ferment it slow and cold with our house yeast strain, using Golden Promise barley and locally milled oats to produce a medium bodied, bready lager. The generous addition of Mandarina Bavaria hops in kettle and during maturation compliments the classic yeast flavours with tangerine, citrus, and spice.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.295453	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
24293	Saison Du Pomme Fresh Gooseberry	5443	Saison	8.0	\N	Keg and bottled, specialIntroducing our new beer Saison du Pomme. This guy has been on the radar for a while, but as usual trying to squeeze more juice out of our brewery is never easy and faced with a busy summer of production the brewplan got delayed a little.  It was the fantastic July weather and the juicy Scottish fruit which we were enjoying  that became the inspiration for this summer harvest  Borders ale.The chosen yeast strain from Belgium’s legendary Brasserie Dupont, was cultured in house and then fermented at elevated temperatures in the traditional style for our recently brewed Farmhouse ale. The aromatic yeast was then harvested and introduced into a high gravity saison, partially fermented with fresh gooseberries from Kelso’s  Rutherford farm and  apple juice from our friends at Thistly Cross Cider shed.   Champagne yeast was then introduced to finish the fermentation under pressure over a period of two weeks, where the fermenting carbon dioxide was captured and packaged up into 500ml bottle and keg.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.295453	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
24296	/ Brewdog Edinburgh Marmalade On Toast	5443	Fruit Beer	6.0	\N	keg, specialBrewed for collaboration fest 2013 between Tempest and Brewdog EdinburghManagement team Fisher and Lynn were sitting merrily on a train, of course having some epic train beers. The creative juices were flowing, a kid brushed past them down the aisle and dropped his Paddington Bear toy, and thus an idea was born! Collaborating with Graeme from Tempest, the Edinburgh team created this marmalade on toast pale ale brewed with orange zest, ginger and bucketloads of toasted malts. - See more at: http://www.brewdog.com/blog-article/brewdog-collab-fest-the-bars-brewdays#sthash.7uGX9sJy.dpuf	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.295453	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
