25066	Thanks Brian!	5449	Saison	8.0	\N	Rye saison. What started as a 12 hour long mistake turned into one of our most unique and amazingly complex creations yet. Since day one our boiler has been an issue. This started as our saison but only simmered in the kettle for 12 hours straight without fully reaching a boil. After scratching our heads at what to do, we decided to toss it into 12yr old Elijah Craig barrels that had just been delivered the day prior. After 10 months we revisited it and boy was it amazing! Huge oak and booze on the nose, transitions to a light acidity and a caramel maltyness. Very unique and one of a kind. We couldn’t make this beer again if we tried!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:48.643807	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
