28137	Dr. Strangematter	5483	Saison	9.6	\N	This Imperial Saison was brewed with holy basil and pink peppercorns from the garden of our Head Brewer Kyle Manns. It’s as homegrown as you can get. We added caramelized wild flower honey from local producer Massey Honey Co. and New Zealand Wakatu and Wai-Iti hops to bring in subtle hints of citrus and tropical fruits. We fermented with authentic French Farmhouse yeast and aged it in Chardonnay barrels that give distinctive flavor and nuance making this beer perfect for a hot day working in the lab. Brewed in collaboration with our friends at Iron Fist Brewing Co., this intricate blend will commemorate the 5th Annual OC Brew Ha Ha Craft Beer festival that runs every September in Orange County, CA.2nd batch released late December 2015 with the following commercial deScription (confirmed to be a rebrew):Something strange is en route to finish out 2015!#Strangematter blurs the lines between beer, mead, and wine -- it’s brewed with pink peppercorns, holy basil, and local orange blossom honey from Massey Farms. Layered notes of oaky tannins and a spirited finish reminiscent of a fine scotch are the beautiful result of a six month rest in Napa Chardonnay barrels. Bottles will be released in 500ml on New Year’s Eve -- when the Tasting Room will be open from 2:00-10:00pm!  This bottle completes our #StasisProject2015 bottle releases -- if you’d like the chance to win this along with the other five incredible barrel aged releases from the past year and simultaneously benefit a great local cause, School on Wheels, Inc., get into the Tasting Room and purchase your raffle tickets!	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:49.659413	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
