29741	Petrus Oud Bruin	5498	Oud Bruin	5.5	\N	Dark ruby red – red as wine. The style is also called the Burgundy of Flanders, and is a very typical and common beer in West FlandersCreated by a secret blend of the aged and sour ‘mother beer’ with fresh brewed sweeter beer, this beer produces a sour-sweet balance, set off by the underlying bitterness of the hops. A discovery! The best in its style! Light in alcohol, exciting complex flavors and tastes come to the forefront.Although serving cold is recommended, taking time to drink it will release more aromas towards the end of your glass.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29743	Petrus Brewmaster'S Selection: Wild Tripel Ale	5498	Tripel	8.0	\N	The Brewmaster’s Selection Wild Tripel Ale is an audacious combination of craftsmanship and experience. 2 American hops, Amarillo and Cascade, are added to our well known Petrus Tripel to enhance the character and aroma. On top of this, the brewmaster added 15% of our foederbeer to give it a touch of sourness and fruitiness. This beer is an unprecedented combination of a hoppy tripel and sour foederbeer.  NOTE: Sometimes labeled as 'Wild Tripel Hop'.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
