29938	Birra di natale	1019	Specialty Grain	6.9	\N	Birra ad alta fermentazione dal colore ambrato prodotta esclusivamente per accompagnare il periodo delle feste natalizie. La Birra di Natale presenta alla vista un colore ambrato tendente all'arancio, è caratterizzata dalle note fruttate e speziate della scorza d'arancia, della noce moscata e della cannella. Corpo strutturato, pieno ed avvolgente, la inseriscono di diritto nelle nostre Birre Speciali.\r\n\r\nOttima per accompagnare, ad esempio i dolci tipici delle festività di Natale, è anche una birra ideale da gustare in ogni momento della giornata. Si consiglia la consumazione ad una temperatura di circa 10° in ampi calici a chiudere in modo che possano essere esaltate tutte le caratteristiche organolettiche.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29948	Enough To Make A Mango Sour	5501	Berliner Weisse	5.5	\N	This beer is enough to make a mango sour! Fra spøk til alvor, dette ølet er en berlinerweisse i tradisjonell tysk stil, som vi har tilsatt mango for å gi et fruktig og godt preg. Øl i denne stilen er normalt rundt 3% sterkt, som gjør at vi kaller vår en 'imperial berlinerweisse'.--------------------------------------------------------------This beer is enough to make a mango sour! This beer started as a traditional (kettle-soured) Berliner Weisse, which we then added mango to in order to give it a fruity bump. Beer in this style tends to hover around 3%, which makes our 6% version imperial.Også brygget hos St. Hallvards og Arendals.....det vil nok endres flere ganger. Prosenten varierer også noe	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29949	Salty Surprise	5501	Grodziskie/Gose/Lichtenhainer	4.7	\N	Release the kraken!Salty Surprise er et øl inspirert av den tradisjonelle, tyske stilen Gose. Ølet er selvsagt med en liten twist i form av pasjonsfrukt og fersken. I tillegg til de tradisjonelle tilsetningene salt, koriander og en syrnet mesk. Alt for å skape en fruktig twist på stilen, som gir deg en real sjøsprøyt.Salty Surprise is a beer inspired by the traditional German beer style, gose. The beer (obviously) has a bit of a twist, in the form of passionfruit and peach. This comes in addition to the soured mash and the traditional addition of salt and coriander.Batch #1 (4.5%) brewed 12.2015 at St. Hallvards Bryggeri	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29954	Vanilla Gorilla	5501	Berliner Weisse	2.5	\N	Vanilla Gorilla is a nearly-hypertonic sports Berliner Weisse, only we’ve replaced the milk protein with milk sugar, and substituted salt for enough vanilla pods to tame your inner brute. He’s got the grains to bring the gains, and the yeast to keep you greased, but the sharp lactic tartness is what will really leave you feeling positively shredded.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29956	/ Ska Cervisiska	5501	Spiced Beer	5.8	\N	(English Below) Cervisiska er vårt samarbeid med eminente Ska Brewing Company, fra Durango i Colorado. Cervisiska er brygget med havre, hvete, og vår særegne maltblanding. Ølet er utelukkende humlet med store mengder Citra-humle, og gjæret med gjærstammen Belgian Ardennes. Ølet har så blitt tilsatt saften fra tindved i sekundær, som bidrar til et ekstra fruktig preg.Ølet er best ferskt, men vil også tåle lagring bedre enn en vanlig pale ale. Ølet er også glutenredusert.------------------------Cervisiska is our collaboration brew with the Durango, Colorado-based Ska Brewing Company. Cervisiska is brewed with oats, wheat, and our characteristic malt profile. The beer is then hopped with massive doses of Citra, and then fermented with the Belgian Ardennes yeast strain. We then add juice from sea buckthorn, with lends the beer an extra fruity nose.Cervisiska is best consumed fresh, but it will also tolerate storage better than a normal pale ale. Cervisiska is also gluten reduced. Please note that the beer have been brewed at different locations.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29962	Tatt På Fersken (6.0%)	5501	Blanche	6.0	\N	Belgisk wit brygget med fersken, vanilje og laktose på toppen av de vanlige ingrediensene maltet hvete, flaket hvete, flaket havre, puffet hvete, belgisk gjær, kamille, appelsinskall og koriander.En imperial-wit med trøkk! PS: Dette ølet tar over for 4,7% utgaven som vi faser ut.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29966	Shoryuken	5501	Berliner Weisse	4.7	\N	\N	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29968	Tatt På Fersken (4.7%)	5501	Blanche	4.7	\N	Å nei, noe er i gjære! Appelsin og Fersken har hatt en affære! Resultatet av denne affæren ble en belgisk witbier med flaket hvete, flaket havre, tysk nobelhumle og belgisk gjær som ble piffet opp med koriander, appelsinskall, kamille og deretter rikelig med ferskenpuré i sekundær. Et lyst, friskt og godt øl som er en skikkelig tørsteslukker. Ølet er gjæret i tradisjonell stil i store, åpne gjæringskar før det blir overført til en lukket sekundærtank. Slik at det får den naturlige smaksprofilen og den gode munnfølelsen en belgisk witbier bør ha.----------------------------------------A Belgian witbier with flaked wheat, flaked oats, German noble hops, and Belgian yeast, which is supported by coriander, orange peel, chamomile, and then finished with a massive amount of peach puree thrown in under secondary fermentation. A light, refreshing, and good beer that is an absolute thirst quencher. The beer is fermented according to tradition in big, open fermenters before it is transferred to a secondary tank, such that it gets the natural taste profile and the enjoyable mouthfeel that a Belgian witbier ought to have.This version of Tatt på Fersken has been bottled for release in the Norwegian market (allowing alcoholic beverages only at or below 4.7% abv), with the exception of 4 kegs which have been set aside for special events.The first batch (November 2015) finished at 4.2% abv.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29976	Brad Peat	5501	Barley Wine	9.2	\N	Brad Peat er en engelsk barleywine brygget med laktose, chipotlechili, aroma fra mandel, pekan, valnøtter og lagret på en bladning fra fransk og amerikansk eik. Et øl som virkelig får frem essensen av “nøtter og tørket frukt” som mange forbinder med stilen. Men Brad Peat er en luring, for han er også brygget med røykmalt og chipotlechili, som gir et delikat og moderat preg av chili og røyk, som raskt går over til lette eiketoner.Dette er en helt spesiell barleywine, som ikke er så søt at et blir for mye av det gode. Et virkelig spesielt øl, med så mange smaker at den ikke helt vet hvem den er. br />Brad Peat is an English barleywine brewed with lactose, chipotle peppers, and aroma from almonds, walnuts, and pecans which has been mellowed by a careful soak over French and American oak. This beer is very forward in the nut and fruit aromas generally associated with the style. But Brad Peat is deceptive, because he’s also been brewed with smoked malt and chipotle. This gives it a delicate hint of chili and smoke, which quickly transforms to a more subtle note of oak.This is a unique barleywine -- not so sweet that it gives you too much of the good stuff, but also complex enough that it almost defies deScription.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29994	Florida Cracker	5502	Blanche	5.0	\N	The Cracker Cowboys of Florida were colonial-era settlers, often of Scots-Irish descent, who arrived in Florida when Spain traded their territory of La Florida to the English. The term Cracker in Florida usage relates to the whip these 'cow hunters' used to herd cattle in Florida’s Palmetto Prairies. Called Quáqueros by the Spanish, these hardy and hard working Cracker Cowboys helped to shape the history of Florida, the nation’s oldest cattle raising state. We brew Florida Cracker White ale with unmalted wheat, orange peel and coriander and then ferment it with a French Saison yeast strain to give it a spicy and dry finish. Perfect for a warm day on the Palmetto Prairie.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
29995	Guava Grove Farmhouse Ale	5502	Fruit Beer	8.0	\N	Guava Grove is a farmhouse ale that sees a secondary fermentation on one of Tampa’s favored fruits, guava. Pairs well with fresh fish, mussels, fresh tropical fruits, and earthy cheeses.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
30000	Warmer Winter Winter Warmer	5502	Barley Wine	10.0	\N	We mashed up traditional English-style barley wine-style and old ale winter warmer-style ales with citrusy American hops like Simcoe, Centennial, Columbus, Chinook, Amarillo and, fittingly, Glacier, to create a Floridian Winter Ale.	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1608270586620-248524c67de9?w=200&h=200&fit=crop	\N	2025-07-22 05:54:50.156454	f	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80	https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80
